WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.680
Hey! Come on.
Let's move!


00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:54.807
No!


00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:56.450
- Let me see.
- No!


00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:58.250
Come on. I made you
a special breakfast.


00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.561
You can't cook.


00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:02.246
Hey, Mary, open up!


00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:08.931
You look beautiful.


00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.804
I look like a Disney character.


00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.004
Where's the "special"?


00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:23.161
The what?


00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.851
You said you made me
a special breakfast.


00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.964
Please don't make me go.


00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.282
You can keep homeschooling me.


00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:36.856
I've taught you
everything I know.


00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:38.086
But I don't wanna go.


00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.408
Well, I don't wanna go
to work, but I do.


00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:44.449
You don't go to work.
You fix the boats on a dock.


00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:47.561
Okay. It's a poor example,
but you're still going.


00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.320
But what about Fred?


00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:52.447
What about him?


00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:53.656
You won't take care of him.


00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:54.761
You don't like cats.


00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:55.976
I don't like two-eyed cats.


00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.256
Fred, as you know, is monocular.


00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:58.884
Who's gonna throw him
his ping pong ball?


00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.800
Fred's gonna be fine.
No more argument, okay?


00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.405
We've discussed this ad nauseam.


00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:06.921
What's ad nauseam?


00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.320
Oh, you don't know?


00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:09.920
Well, looks like
someone needs school.


00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.045
This is gonna be fun.


00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:21.360
You're gonna meet kids today


00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:23.607
you can borrow money from
the rest of your life.


00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.121
Come on.


00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:32.771
You're gonna be great.


00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:35.606
You know, just...


00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:38.970
I don't know. Try bein' a kid.


00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:58.087
Mmm-mmm.


00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:02.967
Frank!


00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:06.885
Frank, I know you hear me.


00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:11.926
Frank!


00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:31.971
There's still time
for you to undo this nonsense.


00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:34.521
Go get in your car
and go get that child.


00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:36.966
Are you technically allowed to


00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:38.485
use those keys
whenever you want?


00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:40.244
How can you stand there...


00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.656
acting all calm
and everything, Frank,


00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:42.761
and make light of this?


00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:45.603
Now go get her back
before it's too late.


00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:47.856
She gotta get out in the world.


00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:48.960
She has no friends her age.


00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.445
No social skills.


00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.487
She doesn't know
how to be a kid.


00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:56.051
Two nights ago, she told me


00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:57.536
that even if Germany
bails out the euro...


00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:59.881
there could still be
a worldwide depression.


00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:02.680
I was staring at the ceiling
for three hours.


00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:06.401
I'm so worried.


00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.282
Come on, Roberta.


00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:11.566
If you start crying,


00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.280
I'm gonna have to
pretend to start crying.


00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:15.766
Hey.


00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.362
You know, there's something
you could be overlookin'.


00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.326
This could work out.


00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:23.007
Maybe.


00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:26.002
But if anybody takes
that baby away...


00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.441
I'll smother you in your sleep.


00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:30.405
Morning, Fred.


00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:38.728
One plus one is two.


00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.843
That is fact number one
of today.


00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:44.368
Who can tell me
what two plus two is?


00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:45.726
Who's got it?


00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:47.926
- Mmm-hmm?
- Four.


00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.001
Excellent, Donna.


00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:52.004
It is. Two plus two is,
indeed, four.


00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:55.446
Okay, who wants to try
three plus three?


00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:00.050
Three plus three? Really?


00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:02.881
I beg your pardon?


00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:05.523
What kinda school
is this anyway?


00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:07.330
It's the kind of school


00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.607
where students don't speak
without permission.


00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:12.525
All right.
But everyone knows it's six.


00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:16.130
Nobody in this classroom
speaks...


00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:18.681
unless they are called upon.


00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:20.962
Okay? Is everybody clear
on that?


00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.929
Yes, ma'am.


00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:25.606
Good. Mary, can you
stand up please?


00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:28.523
Stand on up. Stand up, babe.


00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:31.566
These questions are for you
because you're so advanced.


00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:35.964
What is nine plus eight?


00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:37.451
17.


00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:40.690
Yeah. Yes, it is.
That's good.


00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:42.960
What is...


00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:44.360
15 plus 17?


00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:45.965
32.


00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.685
Yeah. That is right.


00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:52.401
All right, then.


00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:56.451
Well, what is 57 plus 135?


00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:59.287
192.


00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:04.401
Yeah.


00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:13.321
Can you tell me...


00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:19.123
what 57 multiplied by 135 is?


00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:32.647
Okay.


00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:36.929
Who can tell me what four...


00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:41.205
7,695.


00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:43.604
I don't think
anyone can do that.


00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:48.761
The square root is 87.7.


00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:51.806
And change.


00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:55.809
Now what does ad nauseam mean?


00:06:57.880 --> 00:06:59.609
I have a very strange kid.


00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:01.250
I have 27 strange kids.


00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:02.487
Good morning.


00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:03.936
Good morning, good morning,
good morning.


00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:05.976
That's great, guys,
but take your seats, okay?


00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.241
Oh, God. See ya.


00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:10.406
Good morning, Ms. Stevenson.


00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:11.686
Good morning.


00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:13.569
Mind if I sit in?


00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:14.721
Not at all!


00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:16.370
Okay, class.


00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:17.521
I have a treat for you.


00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:22.970
I would like to introduce you
to our principal, Mrs. Davis.


00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:24.963
Good morning, first graders.


00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:28.249
Good morning, Mrs. Davis.


00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:31.006
Are you ready for a great year?


00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:32.685
Yes!


00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:35.525
Uh... Yes, Mary?


00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:36.881
She's the boss?


00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:40.331
Mrs. Davis is our principal.
Mm-kay...


00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:41.806
Okay. Now I want you


00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:43.296
to get on your phone
and call Frank...


00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:45.243
and tell him to
get me out of here!


00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:52.406
Wait a minute.
That's the dad? I know him.


00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:54.642
I see him at Ferg's
almost every Friday night.


00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:57.122
He's the quiet, damaged hot guy.


00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:01.006
What are you doing at Ferg's
every Friday night?


00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:03.128
Trying to get picked up by him.


00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:10.884
Excuse me? Hi.


00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:13.442
Oh. Look, it's my teacher.


00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:16.331
Probably wants to remind me
what one plus one is.


00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:17.447
Go to the car, okay?


00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:19.846
- Hi.
- Hi.


00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:21.536
Sorry to yell at you
and then chase you down.


00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:22.641
It's okay. Mary's teacher?


00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:24.006
Yes. I'm Bonnie Stevenson.


00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:25.640
Frank. How are you?
Sorry about today.


00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:27.171
I know she got
a little overexcited.


00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:28.456
I think
it's just first day jitters.


00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:29.527
Sure. Yeah.


00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:31.256
We're running a little late
actually. We gotta get going.


00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:33.567
Okay. I don't even wanna
talk about that.


00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:35.324
- I'll keep you just a minute.
- Okay.


00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:38.327
I think your daughter...


00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:40.801
I think Mary might be gifted.


00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:43.001
What?


00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:47.165
Yeah. Today in Math,
she answered some really...


00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:49.084
- Oh, no, no, no. That's...
- No, please.


00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:50.416
- It's not gifted.
- Really difficult questions.


00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:51.487
All right.


00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:52.856
Just that
a seven-year-old would...


00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:54.086
It's Trachtenberg.


00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:57.128
- Jakow Trachtenberg.
- I'm sorry?


00:08:57.280 --> 00:08:59.487
Spent seven years
in a Nazi concentration camp.


00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:02.524
Developed a system
to rapidly solve problems.


00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:04.805
It's the Trachtenberg method.


00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:07.326
But she's...


00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:09.882
I mean, she's seven though.


00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:11.451
I learned it when I was eight.


00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:13.405
Do I look gifted to you?


00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:16.360
It's kind of gone out of vogue


00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:18.647
since the invention
of the calculator...


00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:21.207
but, uh, I can still win
a drink at a bar using it.


00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:22.841
Sorry for today.


00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:25.163
- Won't happen again.
- Okay.


00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:27.368
Nice to meet you. Bonnie.


00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:28.521
Frank.


00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:51.206
Hmm.


00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:53.096
For the record,
I didn't wanna go


00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:54.724
to the stupid school
in the first place.


00:09:54.880 --> 00:09:56.291
And the boy in the next row


00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:59.045
acts inappropriately
for someone who's a child.


00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:02.324
I'm sorry. I'm still passive
aggressively ignoring you.


00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:05.691
Other kids answer questions.
They don't get into trouble.


00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:08.002
You didn't get in trouble
for answering questions.


00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:09.525
You yelled at the principal.


00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:12.841
You know what? You're gonna
find this interesting.


00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:15.281
So, I googled "first graders
who yell at the principal... "


00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:16.736
and statistically,
you're never gonna


00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:18.125
believe how many kids do it.


00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:19.287
How many?


00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:20.641
None.


00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:27.085
Frank, I'm sorry.
I'm really sorry.


00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:28.480
Yeah, right.


00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:31.288
You can't show off
like that at school.


00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:32.641
I know.


00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:34.680
You promised you wouldn't,
then the first day...


00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.768
I know, I know. I screwed up.


00:10:41.560 --> 00:10:44.325
Do you think maybe
this boat needs a test ride?


00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:48.407
Go get Fred.


00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:51.091
Don't run.


00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:06.642
<i>I listen to the wind
To the wind of my soul</i>


00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:12.204
<i>Where I'll end up Well, I think</i>


00:11:12.280 --> 00:11:15.841
<i>Only God really knows</i>


00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:21.964
<i>I've sat upon the setting sun</i>


00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:27.131
<i>But never, never, never, never</i>


00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:31.169
<i>I never wanted water once</i>


00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:35.089
<i>No, never, never, never</i>


00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:37.811
Fred loves to watch
the sandpipers.


00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:40.729
He thinks he'd like to
catch one...


00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:42.484
but he'd regret it.


00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:45.323
Fred's not a killer.


00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:46.970
He's a lover.


00:11:53.720 --> 00:11:56.644
Would my mom have wanted me
to go to this school?


00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:58.485
I can only guess.


00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:00.921
But I'll tell you what,


00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:02.729
she would have wanted you
to have friends.


00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:04.724
Idiot friends?


00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:08.840
And she'd want you to have
compassion for others.


00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:12.891
Like a cat can have
for a sandpiper.


00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:17.962
But what if they don't like me?


00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:21.286
Then they're idiots.


00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:34.280
Good morning, class.


00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:38.166
Good morning, Ms. Stevenson.


00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:40.166
Good morning, Mary.


00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:46.161
Good morning, Ms. Stevenson.


00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:48.041
Okay, good morning.


00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:53.971
Get a hold of yourself.


00:12:56.160 --> 00:12:58.447
For my Show and Tell, I have...


00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:00.921
the most awesome cat
in the history of time.


00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:04.529
Not only
is his name Fred, but...


00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:11.204
He has just one eye.


00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:13.408
Uno. Go ahead and count...


00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:16.763
but I promise you,
it's always one.


00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:18.445
How did he lose his eye?


00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:21.847
I don't know. I wasn't there.


00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.445
Just found him
inside of a trash can


00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:26.524
next to a bottle of alcohol
or something.


00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:29.889
He is a smart, smart cat,
but no one realizes that.


00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:33.684
No one understands him.
No one.


00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:37.607
Put your name
on the top of the paper...


00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:40.730
so that I know
who did such good work.


00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.120
I left my pen with you.


00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:43.611
Pass those around, guys.


00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:45.290
Okay? I wanna see your work.


00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:47.488
Turn around, face the desk.


00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:50.288
Think about
how you get to the answer.


00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:54.286
It's not just about,
you know, guessing.


00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:55.851
Don't be messy.


00:13:56.760 --> 00:13:57.807
Done.


00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:09.526
Let's see.


00:14:11.840 --> 00:14:13.171
Mmm-hmm.


00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:16.130
Okay. I thought
you might finish quickly,


00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:17.690
so a little something extra.


00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:08.521
Done.


00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:05.206
Oh...


00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:46.326
Do you know who I am?


00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:49.967
Hey! Mary's teacher...


00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:52.241
Bonnie.


00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:54.004
You lied to me.


00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:56.086
Okay.


00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:58.123
- Can you narrow it down?
- Mmm-hmm.


00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:01.523
I'd like to know the truth
about Mary, my student...


00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:03.682
your niece.


00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:08.326
I was running


00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:09.686
ridiculously late for a date...


00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:11.928
and my sister showed up
with Mary.


00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:13.764
And she never just
showed up unannounced.


00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:15.365
She never showed up
with the baby.


00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:19.203
She said she wanted to talk.


00:17:20.440 --> 00:17:22.010
She said she needed to talk.


00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:24.927
I told her I would talk to her
when I got back.


00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:27.120
I think I figured showing up
that late to my date...


00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:29.049
would hurt my chances
of gettin' laid.


00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:33.687
Came home that night
and Mary was on the couch...


00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:36.525
and found Diane
on the bathroom floor.


00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:40.968
I mean, there's no way
I coulda known...


00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:43.604
but I shoulda known.


00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:46.486
Six and a half years later,


00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:48.085
me and Mary
are still hangin' out.


00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:50.688
And what about the father?


00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:54.284
Diane was so socially awkward...


00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:57.171
she didn't date enough to know
a good guy from a bad guy.


00:17:57.320 --> 00:17:59.800
This particular guy
didn't last a month.


00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:01.644
And no grandparents?


00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:07.767
- Dad died when I was eight.
- My mom...


00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:09.969
Short version is
she turned her back on Diane


00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:11.246
when she got pregnant.


00:18:13.120 --> 00:18:14.121
Why?


00:18:16.520 --> 00:18:18.204
Didn't fit into her plan.


00:18:19.480 --> 00:18:22.131
She's an exacting woman,
my mother.


00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:24.089
Uncompromising.


00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:27.206
Very British.


00:18:27.360 --> 00:18:30.125
Do you mean,
British in demeanor or...


00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:32.362
- No. Like she's...
- She's from England.


00:18:32.520 --> 00:18:34.204
From England. Yeah.


00:18:39.440 --> 00:18:42.444
So, Mary is a genius?


00:19:15.120 --> 00:19:16.451
Oh!


00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:19.125
Look out. Look out.


00:19:19.280 --> 00:19:22.045
Your little animals
are escaping, dumbass.


00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:25.124
Hey! You should not
be laughing!


00:19:25.960 --> 00:19:28.361
You did a mean thing
to a little kid!


00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:30.085
What are you gonna do about it?


00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:53.171
Hey, you okay?


00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:56.724
You good? All right.


00:19:58.240 --> 00:19:59.810
How do we resolve this?


00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:01.484
You know, she could be expelled.


00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:04.367
God. I hope not.


00:20:04.520 --> 00:20:06.727
But if every other first-time
offender was expelled,


00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:07.881
I guess fair is fair.


00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:09.724
Are you gonna
take this seriously?


00:20:09.880 --> 00:20:13.487
Sure. You don't bluff me,
I don't bluff you.


00:20:15.920 --> 00:20:17.649
Ms. Stevenson believes


00:20:17.720 --> 00:20:19.688
that your child
is exceptional...


00:20:19.840 --> 00:20:22.446
and has talents
that our curriculum


00:20:22.520 --> 00:20:24.045
can't begin to challenge.


00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:26.004
It just so happens


00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:28.248
that I am good friends
with the headmaster


00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:31.131
of the Oaks Academy
for Gifted Education.


00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:32.520
He has always said


00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:34.568
that if I find
that one in a million...


00:20:34.720 --> 00:20:37.724
And the one in a million
has a $30,000 tuition.


00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:40.528
Mr. Adler, I can get
your daughter a scholarship.


00:20:40.680 --> 00:20:41.761
Full ride.


00:20:42.080 --> 00:20:43.923
I wouldn't say it
if I couldn't do it.


00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:59.723
I realize, putting that girl
in that setting,


00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:02.929
you know, 99 times out of
a 100, that's what you do.


00:21:03.080 --> 00:21:04.445
It's the Oaks.
It's a great school.


00:21:04.520 --> 00:21:05.681
I looked into it.


00:21:06.560 --> 00:21:08.847
But this family has a history
with those schools.


00:21:10.440 --> 00:21:12.727
And I think the last thing
that little girl needs


00:21:12.880 --> 00:21:15.326
is reinforcement
that she's different.


00:21:16.280 --> 00:21:18.282
Trust me, she knows. So...


00:21:20.560 --> 00:21:24.246
I think Mary,
I think she's gotta be here.


00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:27.683
Today's a bad ending.
You can't hit people.


00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:29.964
But a 12-year-old
bullies a seven-year-old


00:21:30.040 --> 00:21:31.371
and she stands up?


00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:34.136
Do you know how important
it is to me that she did that?


00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:36.367
You know how proud I am
of her? Aren't you?


00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:38.847
Mr. Adler, your daughter
shattered a young boy's...


00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:41.207
I know. You can't hit people.


00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:43.323
That will be made very clear.
I get that.


00:21:43.480 --> 00:21:46.131
But Mrs. Davis,
if we separate our leaders,


00:21:46.320 --> 00:21:49.767
if we segregate them
from people like you and me,


00:21:49.920 --> 00:21:51.922
you get congressmen.


00:21:53.520 --> 00:21:54.521
So, I'm sorry.


00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:56.489
I wish I could take
your offer, but Mary stays.


00:21:56.640 --> 00:21:57.721
Unless you kick her out.


00:21:57.920 --> 00:22:00.730
This is a mistake. We'll never
be able to raise this child


00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:03.526
to the level of scholarship
she deserves.


00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:08.811
Well, just dumb her down
into a decent human being.


00:22:09.320 --> 00:22:10.401
Everybody wins.


00:22:15.560 --> 00:22:18.609
You know what?
Can you excuse me one minute?


00:22:19.560 --> 00:22:21.289
Bring me
every piece of paperwork


00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:22.765
we have on this girl.


00:22:24.960 --> 00:22:25.961
Hey.


00:22:29.320 --> 00:22:31.527
Are you sure
you know what you're doing?


00:22:35.520 --> 00:22:36.521
No.


00:22:42.760 --> 00:22:43.921
Okay. Mary, I think


00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:45.656
you have something you'd like
to say to the class.


00:22:45.680 --> 00:22:47.921
You wanna hop up and say it?


00:22:53.640 --> 00:22:56.644
Okay. I'm supposed to
say something.


00:22:57.080 --> 00:23:01.165
Hitting people is wrong
even if they're bad.


00:23:01.320 --> 00:23:05.211
I won't do it again,
so don't be afraid of me.


00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:09.768
Okay. Thank you.


00:23:09.920 --> 00:23:12.366
Now can I say something
I wanna say?


00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:14.121
Sure.


00:23:15.520 --> 00:23:17.170
Before they ruined it,


00:23:17.320 --> 00:23:19.891
Justin's zoo
was the best art project.


00:23:21.360 --> 00:23:24.091
By far. It was awesome.


00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:29.843
Come on. A little harder.


00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:33.047
Okay.


00:23:34.480 --> 00:23:37.370
Thank you. Thank you.


00:23:43.720 --> 00:23:46.121
There's a lady standing
in front of our door.


00:23:46.320 --> 00:23:47.367
Who is it?


00:23:47.520 --> 00:23:49.727
How should I know? I'm seven.


00:23:53.680 --> 00:23:55.842
That would be your grandmother.


00:23:56.560 --> 00:23:59.325
Holy shit!


00:24:01.880 --> 00:24:04.201
An Apple? Whoa.


00:24:05.600 --> 00:24:07.443
It's a MacBook, darling.


00:24:07.600 --> 00:24:10.001
Top of the line
with the Retina Display.


00:24:10.160 --> 00:24:13.004
Hey, you know who else
has a Retina Display?


00:24:13.080 --> 00:24:14.127
Fred!


00:24:14.800 --> 00:24:18.168
Mary, I understand
you like mathematics.


00:24:18.320 --> 00:24:20.129
So, on there,


00:24:20.280 --> 00:24:21.361
you'll find a great


00:24:21.480 --> 00:24:23.926
out-of-print book
by Charles Zimmer


00:24:24.200 --> 00:24:26.680
<i>called Transitions
in Advanced Algebra.</i>


00:24:27.280 --> 00:24:29.442
Yeah. Love that book.


00:24:31.240 --> 00:24:32.526
You're saying you've read it?


00:24:32.680 --> 00:24:35.809
Yeah. I've kind of moved on
to differential equations now.


00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:39.128
Don't forget your manners.
Thank your grandma.


00:24:39.280 --> 00:24:40.520
Thank you, Grandma.


00:24:40.680 --> 00:24:43.411
Grandmother or Evelyn
will do just fine.


00:24:44.680 --> 00:24:47.365
There's so much more on there.


00:24:47.520 --> 00:24:49.284
Things I know you'll find
really challenging.


00:24:49.440 --> 00:24:51.044
Yes. But sadly,
it's a school night


00:24:51.120 --> 00:24:52.451
and there's homework to do.


00:24:52.600 --> 00:24:54.967
What a surprise though, right?


00:24:55.120 --> 00:24:56.963
Say good night
to Grandmother or Evelyn.


00:24:57.760 --> 00:24:59.125
Good night.


00:24:59.680 --> 00:25:01.728
I'd kill a priest
for a Benadryl.


00:25:01.880 --> 00:25:03.211
Still with the allergies?


00:25:03.360 --> 00:25:05.203
Why in God's name
have you got a cat?


00:25:05.280 --> 00:25:06.441
You don't even like cats.


00:25:06.600 --> 00:25:08.204
It's not my cat.
It's Mary's cat.


00:25:08.280 --> 00:25:09.691
I'm just along for the ride.


00:25:09.760 --> 00:25:10.841
So let me guess.


00:25:10.920 --> 00:25:12.570
Our lovely principal,
Ms. Davis.


00:25:12.720 --> 00:25:14.961
Never get on the bad side
of small-minded people


00:25:15.120 --> 00:25:16.485
who have a little authority.


00:25:16.640 --> 00:25:18.290
I thought I taught you that.


00:25:19.880 --> 00:25:21.041
What are you doin' here?


00:25:21.120 --> 00:25:22.256
You don't think I have the right


00:25:22.280 --> 00:25:23.327
to see my granddaughter?


00:25:23.400 --> 00:25:25.767
I do. I'm thrilled your
seven-year exhaustive search


00:25:25.960 --> 00:25:28.327
has finally come
to a fruitful conclusion.


00:25:29.160 --> 00:25:32.130
I don't think this is
an appropriate time to talk.


00:25:32.280 --> 00:25:33.406
Certainly not the setting.


00:25:33.560 --> 00:25:35.562
While I was waiting,
a cockroach this big


00:25:35.640 --> 00:25:37.449
tried to steal my shoe.


00:25:37.640 --> 00:25:39.608
Yeah. They'll take a shoe.


00:25:41.320 --> 00:25:43.641
Honestly, this?


00:25:43.800 --> 00:25:47.646
This godforsaken mosquito
ranch was a conscious choice?


00:25:49.360 --> 00:25:51.761
I could drop you back off
at the airport.


00:26:13.520 --> 00:26:16.842
This thing is loaded
with cool problems.


00:26:25.720 --> 00:26:27.563
So, are you teaching?


00:26:27.720 --> 00:26:28.960
I repair boats.


00:26:29.280 --> 00:26:31.681
- Please.
- I'm not bad at it either.


00:26:31.840 --> 00:26:33.604
Well, then, that explains this.


00:26:33.760 --> 00:26:35.888
They don't sell sunscreen here?


00:26:36.040 --> 00:26:37.087
I wear sunscreen.


00:26:37.280 --> 00:26:39.487
<i>Not enough.
And you need a hat.</i>


00:26:39.640 --> 00:26:42.405
A big hat that shades
your face and neck.


00:26:42.560 --> 00:26:44.336
You're playing Russian
roulette with your skin.


00:26:44.360 --> 00:26:45.691
You look like a porn producer.


00:26:45.840 --> 00:26:48.366
Okay. I appreciate the advice.
I do.


00:26:48.520 --> 00:26:50.416
But we're not here to talk
about sunscreen, are we?


00:26:50.440 --> 00:26:53.205
Oh, so no more small talk?
That's a shame.


00:26:53.720 --> 00:26:56.929
Okay. The environment you have
created for that child


00:26:57.080 --> 00:26:58.809
where she lives,
the school she attends,


00:26:58.880 --> 00:27:00.200
it's substandard,
every bit of it.


00:27:00.280 --> 00:27:01.645
I disagree.


00:27:01.720 --> 00:27:02.767
We're getting nowhere


00:27:02.840 --> 00:27:03.976
if we're not gonna be honest
with each other.


00:27:04.000 --> 00:27:05.764
I am being honest.


00:27:05.920 --> 00:27:09.322
I see. Fine. Well, I'm not
leaving without her.


00:27:09.520 --> 00:27:12.126
Well, welcome to Florida.


00:27:12.280 --> 00:27:14.442
Frank, please listen to reason.


00:27:14.600 --> 00:27:16.921
At some point, either you're
gonna come to the conclusion,


00:27:17.000 --> 00:27:18.081
or someone in authority


00:27:18.160 --> 00:27:19.296
is going to spell it out for you


00:27:19.320 --> 00:27:21.607
that the child's best interest
is all that matters.


00:27:21.760 --> 00:27:24.127
You're gonna make me
pull rank, I will.


00:27:24.280 --> 00:27:25.691
Diane didn't want you
to have her.


00:27:26.440 --> 00:27:27.566
Diane...


00:27:29.360 --> 00:27:31.169
Diane didn't always
think things through.


00:27:31.320 --> 00:27:33.256
Arguably one of the brightest
minds on the planet.


00:27:33.280 --> 00:27:34.520
Good luck going down that road.


00:27:34.600 --> 00:27:35.816
And what do you think she'd say


00:27:35.840 --> 00:27:37.968
if she saw
how her child is living now?


00:27:38.120 --> 00:27:40.043
Do you honestly think
she'd be pleased?


00:27:40.200 --> 00:27:42.726
That she's living a somewhat
normal life? Yes. I do.


00:27:42.880 --> 00:27:44.848
She's not normal.
And treating her as such...


00:27:45.000 --> 00:27:46.729
is negligence on a grand scale.


00:27:47.000 --> 00:27:49.401
I know your heart's
in the right place on this.


00:27:49.960 --> 00:27:53.123
But you are denying the girl
her potential. You are.


00:27:54.040 --> 00:27:56.247
I can provide for her,
I can enrich her life.


00:27:56.360 --> 00:27:58.283
Oh, come on, Evelyn.
You're gonna take that girl,


00:27:58.360 --> 00:27:59.496
you're gonna bury her
in tutors...


00:27:59.520 --> 00:28:01.376
then you're gonna loan her
out to some think tank...


00:28:01.400 --> 00:28:02.970
where she can talk
non-trivial zeros...


00:28:03.160 --> 00:28:05.136
with a bunch of old Russian
guys for the rest of her life.


00:28:05.160 --> 00:28:06.969
And you'd bury her under a rock.


00:28:07.160 --> 00:28:08.650
Look, I don't expect you
to understand


00:28:08.720 --> 00:28:10.280
the price you have to pay
for greatness.


00:28:10.360 --> 00:28:13.364
Oh, I do. That's why I have
Mary in the first place.


00:28:13.840 --> 00:28:15.251
That's uncalled for.


00:28:15.400 --> 00:28:17.641
Your sister had
a laundry list of problems.


00:28:17.720 --> 00:28:19.016
She could have solved
Navier-Stokes


00:28:19.040 --> 00:28:20.120
and gone down in history...


00:28:20.160 --> 00:28:22.120
as one of the greatest
mathematicians of all time.


00:28:22.160 --> 00:28:24.367
But she didn't because
she couldn't finish.


00:28:24.520 --> 00:28:25.965
She was weak.


00:28:26.040 --> 00:28:27.929
Weak like her father
and weak like...


00:28:32.240 --> 00:28:33.321
Well...


00:28:33.640 --> 00:28:35.642
Now, if it's who I think
it is...


00:28:36.280 --> 00:28:38.362
Kinda puts a black cloud
over our luncheon.


00:28:38.520 --> 00:28:41.330
You're still stubborn
and vindictive.


00:28:42.360 --> 00:28:43.646
Careful, Mother.


00:28:43.800 --> 00:28:46.201
There's an apple and tree
analogy lurking.


00:28:46.880 --> 00:28:48.644
You guys ready to order?


00:28:49.160 --> 00:28:50.844
Here's an idea.


00:28:51.040 --> 00:28:52.804
Stop thinking about me
and you...


00:28:53.000 --> 00:28:55.287
and start thinking about
what's best for the child.


00:28:55.760 --> 00:28:59.003
For any reasonable person,
a clear picture will emerge.


00:28:59.360 --> 00:29:02.045
If it doesn't, I suggest
you call your attorney.


00:29:05.040 --> 00:29:07.202
He'll have the bucket of beer.


00:29:36.520 --> 00:29:38.329
Hey, let's go outside.


00:29:40.400 --> 00:29:41.481
No.


00:29:42.880 --> 00:29:44.609
Come on. It's nice out.


00:29:44.920 --> 00:29:47.207
I don't care.


00:29:53.640 --> 00:29:56.291
Hey, no more math today.


00:30:08.800 --> 00:30:10.245
Is there a God?


00:30:10.400 --> 00:30:11.731
I don't know.


00:30:11.880 --> 00:30:13.166
Just tell me.


00:30:13.320 --> 00:30:15.084
I would if I could.


00:30:15.240 --> 00:30:17.846
But I don't know.
And neither does anybody else.


00:30:18.040 --> 00:30:19.610
Roberta knows.


00:30:19.760 --> 00:30:22.161
No.
Roberta has faith


00:30:22.320 --> 00:30:23.845
and that's a great thing
to have.


00:30:24.000 --> 00:30:25.843
But faith's about
what you think, feel.


00:30:25.920 --> 00:30:27.251
Not what you know.


00:30:27.720 --> 00:30:29.404
What about Jesus?


00:30:29.560 --> 00:30:31.767
Love that guy.
Do what he says.


00:30:31.920 --> 00:30:33.922
But is he God?


00:30:35.160 --> 00:30:36.605
I don't know.


00:30:36.760 --> 00:30:38.205
I have an opinion.


00:30:38.360 --> 00:30:40.522
But that's my opinion.
I could be wrong.


00:30:40.680 --> 00:30:42.409
So why would I screw up yours?


00:30:43.840 --> 00:30:45.126
Use your head.


00:30:45.320 --> 00:30:47.687
But don't be afraid
to believe in things either.


00:30:51.600 --> 00:30:53.728
Huh.
There was a guy on TV


00:30:53.800 --> 00:30:55.404
who said there was no God.


00:30:56.800 --> 00:30:57.961
The only difference


00:30:58.040 --> 00:30:59.640
between the atheists on TV
and Roberta...


00:30:59.680 --> 00:31:01.921
is that Roberta loves you.
She's trying to help.


00:31:03.600 --> 00:31:05.125
Tell you what though.


00:31:05.800 --> 00:31:06.847
One way or another,


00:31:06.920 --> 00:31:08.968
we all end up back together
in the end.


00:31:09.600 --> 00:31:11.364
That's what
you're asking, right?


00:31:13.280 --> 00:31:14.361
Yep.


00:31:14.760 --> 00:31:15.841
Okay.


00:31:16.400 --> 00:31:18.641
Find something else
to worry about, will you?


00:31:19.240 --> 00:31:20.446
All right.


00:31:24.720 --> 00:31:27.530
Okay. Adler,
grandmother and uncle.


00:31:28.760 --> 00:31:29.886
Really?


00:31:31.840 --> 00:31:33.285
You sure you folks
don't wanna go out


00:31:33.360 --> 00:31:34.600
in the hallway and settle this?


00:31:38.320 --> 00:31:40.243
No? Well, that's a shame.


00:31:40.800 --> 00:31:43.041
Mr. Cullen, you are here
for the uncle.


00:31:43.120 --> 00:31:44.360
Yes, sir, Your Honor.


00:31:44.520 --> 00:31:46.010
Start charging you room
and board.


00:31:46.160 --> 00:31:47.207
Mr. Highsmith,


00:31:47.280 --> 00:31:49.160
you're on the wrong side
of the bay, aren't you?


00:31:49.320 --> 00:31:51.971
I'm very happy
to be here, Your Honor.


00:31:52.080 --> 00:31:53.161
For the record,
Mrs. Dibbons


00:31:53.240 --> 00:31:54.576
is representing
the State of Florida


00:31:54.600 --> 00:31:55.840
Child Welfare Department.


00:31:56.000 --> 00:31:57.081
Proceed.


00:31:57.240 --> 00:31:58.969
Your Honor,
my client, Mrs. Adler


00:31:59.040 --> 00:32:00.640
is the maternal grandmother
of the child.


00:32:00.760 --> 00:32:02.091
Her daughter, the girl's mother,


00:32:02.160 --> 00:32:03.207
was a troubled woman...


00:32:03.280 --> 00:32:05.521
who seven years ago,
sadly, took her own life.


00:32:05.680 --> 00:32:07.648
It was at this time
that Mr. Adler


00:32:07.720 --> 00:32:09.165
preemptively and illegally...


00:32:09.360 --> 00:32:10.600
took custody of the girl


00:32:10.680 --> 00:32:12.016
and spirited her
across state lines...


00:32:12.040 --> 00:32:14.407
for the purpose
of denying my client custody.


00:32:14.880 --> 00:32:17.080
Now, there is evidence that
the child currently lives...


00:32:17.160 --> 00:32:20.050
in unclean
and unwholesome conditions.


00:32:20.320 --> 00:32:22.129
We petition the court
to grant my client


00:32:22.200 --> 00:32:23.326
full custody of the child...


00:32:23.480 --> 00:32:24.561
so that she may be returned


00:32:24.640 --> 00:32:25.971
to the state of Massachusetts...


00:32:26.120 --> 00:32:28.487
and given the care
to which she is entitled.


00:32:30.560 --> 00:32:34.042
My client took an infant under
his wing for one reason only.


00:32:34.200 --> 00:32:37.124
It was his sister's desire
that he do so.


00:32:37.280 --> 00:32:39.362
My client has been
her constant caregiver.


00:32:39.560 --> 00:32:41.456
And, Your Honor, as far as
the living conditions...


00:32:41.480 --> 00:32:44.006
I've been in this home.
It's fine.


00:32:44.160 --> 00:32:46.447
I mean, if we adopt standards
based on...


00:32:46.600 --> 00:32:48.536
our northern friend's
aversion to palmetto bugs...


00:32:48.560 --> 00:32:51.086
we won't have a child left
south of Tallahassee.


00:32:55.360 --> 00:32:57.044
All right. Last chance
before this starts


00:32:57.160 --> 00:32:58.810
costing a lot more money.


00:32:58.960 --> 00:33:00.485
Your Honor, my client would need


00:33:00.560 --> 00:33:01.800
reasonable access to the child.


00:33:02.040 --> 00:33:03.201
So ordered.


00:33:03.280 --> 00:33:04.416
Ms. Dibbons,
you'll go over there


00:33:04.440 --> 00:33:05.656
and check out
the living conditions?


00:33:05.680 --> 00:33:06.727
On the books, Your Honor.


00:33:06.920 --> 00:33:08.524
All right, folks.
Drive carefully.


00:33:10.880 --> 00:33:12.245
Her lawyer has a nice suit.


00:33:13.240 --> 00:33:16.449
Relax, Frank. More weight's
put on the talent competition.


00:33:17.200 --> 00:33:18.611
Go have a cocktail, hmm?


00:33:20.400 --> 00:33:23.290
Roberta, would you
like to have Mary tonight?


00:33:23.880 --> 00:33:26.121
Why wouldn't I like
to have Mary tonight?


00:33:27.760 --> 00:33:29.683
I told you something like this
would happen.


00:33:30.120 --> 00:33:31.451
Now look where we are.


00:33:32.760 --> 00:33:34.416
And I'm supposed to believe
you know what you're doing.


00:33:34.440 --> 00:33:35.920
You couldn't even find
a white lawyer.


00:33:36.880 --> 00:33:38.769
Wow. Look, just...


00:33:39.400 --> 00:33:41.040
- Don't worry, okay?
- Don't tell me that.


00:33:41.200 --> 00:33:42.122
There's nothing you can say


00:33:42.200 --> 00:33:43.456
that's gonna make me
feel good...


00:33:43.480 --> 00:33:45.448
because I have no say
in any of this, Frank.


00:33:45.600 --> 00:33:46.726
I'm not a blood relative,


00:33:46.800 --> 00:33:48.450
I'm not a legal guardian.
I'm nothing!


00:33:48.680 --> 00:33:50.011
Just the lady
who lives next door,


00:33:50.080 --> 00:33:51.176
whose opinion means nothing...


00:33:51.200 --> 00:33:52.964
whose feelings mean nothing.


00:33:53.880 --> 00:33:56.360
Would I like to have
Mary tonight?


00:33:56.760 --> 00:33:59.081
I'd like to have Mary
every night.


00:34:05.320 --> 00:34:08.403
<i>Can't stop me now
Hear what I say</i>


00:34:10.200 --> 00:34:11.770
<i>My feet's gotta move, so...</i>


00:34:11.920 --> 00:34:13.570
<i>Get out of my way</i>


00:34:13.720 --> 00:34:15.802
<i>I'm gonna have my say</i>


00:34:15.960 --> 00:34:18.804
<i>I'm going to every discotheque</i>


00:34:18.960 --> 00:34:21.850
<i>I'm gonna dance, dance, dance
Whoo!</i>


00:34:21.920 --> 00:34:23.126
<i>Till the break of day</i>


00:34:23.280 --> 00:34:26.727
<i>Oh, shame, shame, shame, shame</i>


00:34:26.840 --> 00:34:27.887
<i>Oh!</i>


00:34:28.000 --> 00:34:30.002
<i>Shame on you</i>


00:34:30.160 --> 00:34:31.491
<i>If you can't dance too</i>


00:34:32.600 --> 00:34:35.763
<i>And I said shame, shame,
shame, shame</i>


00:34:35.920 --> 00:34:38.685
<i>Shame, shame, shame Shame on you</i>


00:34:48.280 --> 00:34:49.361
Hi.


00:34:51.760 --> 00:34:52.761
Hi.


00:34:54.920 --> 00:34:58.402
Um, I heard Davis bragging
about a custody case


00:34:58.480 --> 00:34:59.925
and then I found out whose...


00:35:01.280 --> 00:35:02.611
I feel terrible.


00:35:02.680 --> 00:35:04.760
But I also wanted you to know
that after we talked...


00:35:04.800 --> 00:35:06.564
I didn't say anything to anyone.


00:35:06.720 --> 00:35:08.529
I swear.


00:35:08.680 --> 00:35:11.923
And it's, um, important to me
that you know that.


00:35:12.960 --> 00:35:14.041
I know.


00:35:16.880 --> 00:35:17.881
Okay.


00:35:18.040 --> 00:35:20.202
My lawyer told me to get drunk.


00:35:22.760 --> 00:35:24.200
And you're trying to do it
with that?


00:35:29.760 --> 00:35:31.364
Okay. My turn.


00:35:32.880 --> 00:35:34.882
Who was your first
celebrity crush?


00:35:35.400 --> 00:35:38.483
Um, I'll go with...


00:35:38.640 --> 00:35:40.608
<i>Mona from Who's the Boss?</i>


00:35:40.680 --> 00:35:41.727
Oh, wow!


00:35:41.800 --> 00:35:42.896
You know who I'm talking about?


00:35:42.920 --> 00:35:44.416
- The sexy grandmother.
- Yeah!


00:35:44.440 --> 00:35:45.840
I always felt like
she had a secret.


00:35:45.880 --> 00:35:48.121
Yeah, which is that
she loved sexual intercourse.


00:35:48.200 --> 00:35:49.201
That was it.


00:35:49.280 --> 00:35:50.416
And she wasn't secret about it.


00:35:50.440 --> 00:35:52.841
That's why I liked her.


00:35:53.320 --> 00:35:54.890
You know what?
I liked her, too.


00:35:55.080 --> 00:35:56.241
See?


00:35:57.240 --> 00:35:59.049
All right. Um...


00:35:59.600 --> 00:36:02.080
Least favorite student.
And why.


00:36:02.480 --> 00:36:03.891
Oh, no!
I love all my students.


00:36:04.040 --> 00:36:07.487
I don't believe you.
At all! Not for a second.


00:36:07.680 --> 00:36:08.920
No, they're all great.


00:36:09.080 --> 00:36:10.809
They're all so great.


00:36:12.360 --> 00:36:14.124
I'm gonna go ahead and drink.


00:36:14.280 --> 00:36:15.770
Let's keep this honest.


00:36:15.920 --> 00:36:17.206
He? She?


00:36:17.320 --> 00:36:19.209
Uh, he is Ronnie Middleton.


00:36:19.800 --> 00:36:21.325
Sounds like a dick.


00:36:22.880 --> 00:36:25.167
- He's a little child, okay?
- I'm sorry.


00:36:25.320 --> 00:36:27.971
The point is that he's evil
in his core.


00:36:30.360 --> 00:36:32.089
And there's nothing I can do.


00:36:32.240 --> 00:36:33.730
Wow.


00:36:39.800 --> 00:36:41.290
What's your greatest fear?


00:36:42.520 --> 00:36:43.726
Wow!


00:36:43.880 --> 00:36:44.927
That's a change of tone.


00:36:45.080 --> 00:36:46.844
Yup, I'm a really
serious person.


00:36:47.000 --> 00:36:48.331
Okay.


00:36:49.280 --> 00:36:51.965
Look, if it's too much, you
can just drink your drink...


00:36:52.680 --> 00:36:54.967
and live with the fact
that you're afraid.


00:36:55.120 --> 00:36:56.963
No, I can handle this. Um...


00:37:01.960 --> 00:37:03.530
That I'll ruin Mary's life.


00:37:15.800 --> 00:37:17.484
You're very, um...


00:37:18.520 --> 00:37:21.569
surprising, Mary's teacher.


00:37:21.920 --> 00:37:23.126
Very much so.


00:37:29.000 --> 00:37:31.606
- Okay. Hold on. I'm sorry.
- What?


00:37:31.760 --> 00:37:33.250
Just so that...


00:37:33.400 --> 00:37:35.368
I feel like
I need to say this...


00:37:35.560 --> 00:37:37.449
just so that
there's no misconception.


00:37:37.600 --> 00:37:38.681
Oh, God. No, I didn't...


00:37:38.840 --> 00:37:39.887
No, hold on!


00:37:40.040 --> 00:37:42.884
That this can't,
isn't happening.


00:37:43.040 --> 00:37:45.327
I get it. I know.
I'm with you.


00:37:45.480 --> 00:37:47.608
- Yeah? Okay.
- 100%. We're on the same page.


00:37:47.760 --> 00:37:48.841
Good!


00:37:49.600 --> 00:37:52.809
No, that's great. I'm sorry.
That's embarrassing.


00:37:52.960 --> 00:37:54.530
It's okay. I get it.


00:37:58.480 --> 00:37:59.527
Oh!


00:37:59.600 --> 00:38:01.523
- Are you okay?
- Yeah, I'm good.


00:38:01.600 --> 00:38:02.647
Okay. Good.


00:38:03.880 --> 00:38:05.450
Can you promise
that there's no way?


00:38:05.600 --> 00:38:07.284
Yes. Roberta has Mary


00:38:07.360 --> 00:38:08.536
every Saturday till noon,
I promise.


00:38:08.560 --> 00:38:10.483
- Yeah?
- Mmm-hmm.


00:38:13.120 --> 00:38:16.283
Mmm. Mmm-mmm. Sorry.


00:38:16.480 --> 00:38:18.687
I can't do this.


00:38:20.680 --> 00:38:23.570
Okay.


00:38:24.640 --> 00:38:25.766
Okay.


00:38:27.120 --> 00:38:28.406
I understand.


00:38:29.840 --> 00:38:31.001
I'll take you home.


00:38:31.200 --> 00:38:32.929
Yeah.


00:38:33.120 --> 00:38:36.090
Sorry, just... One more time.


00:38:53.560 --> 00:38:55.801
I can't find my DVD.


00:38:55.960 --> 00:38:57.610
It's right there, baby.


00:38:57.760 --> 00:38:59.489
No, it isn't.
You come and find it.


00:38:59.640 --> 00:39:00.926
I'm doing lady business.


00:39:01.080 --> 00:39:02.456
Now, you were the last person
to watch it.


00:39:02.480 --> 00:39:03.527
What did you do with it?


00:39:07.120 --> 00:39:08.360
Oh...


00:39:37.160 --> 00:39:38.286
Oh! Oh, my God!


00:39:48.440 --> 00:39:51.569
Good morning, Miss Stevenson.


00:39:52.800 --> 00:39:54.006
Hi.


00:39:55.800 --> 00:39:56.847
Look, I am...


00:39:56.920 --> 00:39:58.536
Oh, you know what?
I'm actually incapable...


00:39:58.560 --> 00:40:00.608
of having
this conversation right now.


00:40:00.760 --> 00:40:02.967
Good. 'Cause I have no idea
what I was gonna say.


00:40:04.560 --> 00:40:06.369
Great! Perfect!


00:40:06.520 --> 00:40:09.569
Sir, if you please.
Take me to jail.


00:40:18.080 --> 00:40:19.445
Awkward.


00:40:20.800 --> 00:40:21.801
Mary...


00:40:21.960 --> 00:40:23.041
Stop! Stop!


00:40:23.200 --> 00:40:25.282
Stop with the Legos! Listen.


00:40:25.480 --> 00:40:27.130
Do we have a rule
about Saturday morning?


00:40:27.320 --> 00:40:28.526
What?


00:40:29.360 --> 00:40:30.496
Are you allowed
in this apartment this early


00:40:30.520 --> 00:40:31.720
on Saturday morning?
Yes or no?


00:40:31.840 --> 00:40:33.444
- No.
- No!


00:40:34.960 --> 00:40:36.166
Are you allowed to... Hey!


00:40:36.320 --> 00:40:38.561
Stop! Enough with the Legos.


00:40:38.720 --> 00:40:40.643
Are you allowed to
use Roberta's keys?


00:40:40.800 --> 00:40:42.006
- No.
- No!


00:40:42.760 --> 00:40:45.161
Hey! Look at me.


00:40:45.320 --> 00:40:47.607
Then why are you here, huh?


00:40:48.200 --> 00:40:49.361
Can you answer me that?


00:40:49.600 --> 00:40:51.409
You broke every rule!


00:40:52.480 --> 00:40:54.608
You just embarrassed me.


00:40:54.800 --> 00:40:55.926
We have these rules.


00:40:56.080 --> 00:40:58.128
We've gone over them
a hundred times! Ahh!


00:40:59.240 --> 00:41:00.685
God!


00:41:00.840 --> 00:41:02.410
Damn it!


00:41:02.600 --> 00:41:04.682
Can I just get five minutes
of my own life?


00:41:34.120 --> 00:41:36.282
Nothing that happened today
was your fault.


00:41:36.440 --> 00:41:38.044
I got mad at you...


00:41:38.200 --> 00:41:40.009
I was really mad at me.


00:41:40.920 --> 00:41:42.684
<i>And the manufacturers oi Legos,</i>


00:41:42.760 --> 00:41:44.125
they should all be in prison.


00:41:48.680 --> 00:41:50.125
I'm sorry.


00:41:52.080 --> 00:41:53.445
Do you forgive me?


00:41:54.640 --> 00:41:56.130
Sure. Whatever.


00:41:56.760 --> 00:41:59.127
Hey, close the laptop.
Come on.


00:41:59.720 --> 00:42:02.371
Please. Doesn't count
if it's not eye to eye.


00:42:03.520 --> 00:42:05.045
Come on, please.


00:42:08.200 --> 00:42:10.441
Do you really have no life
because of me?


00:42:12.680 --> 00:42:14.250
That's not what I said.


00:42:14.480 --> 00:42:15.891
Hmm.


00:42:16.960 --> 00:42:18.485
Did you mean it?


00:42:21.160 --> 00:42:22.207
Last month you said I was


00:42:22.280 --> 00:42:23.376
the worst uncle in the world...


00:42:23.400 --> 00:42:24.686
and you wished death upon me


00:42:24.760 --> 00:42:26.040
'cause I didn't buy you a piano.


00:42:26.520 --> 00:42:28.010
Did you mean that?


00:42:29.160 --> 00:42:30.605
No.


00:42:30.760 --> 00:42:32.489
Not entirely.


00:42:35.240 --> 00:42:36.287
There you go.


00:42:36.440 --> 00:42:38.920
We say things all the time
we don't mean. So...


00:42:40.680 --> 00:42:42.205
Let's forget it, okay?


00:42:44.280 --> 00:42:45.281
Okay.


00:42:45.920 --> 00:42:47.365
Okay.


00:42:50.960 --> 00:42:52.041
Frank?


00:42:52.200 --> 00:42:53.201
Yeah?


00:42:53.880 --> 00:42:54.881
Can I have a piano?


00:42:55.040 --> 00:42:56.087
No.


00:42:58.000 --> 00:42:59.729
Was that really Mary's teacher
this morning?


00:43:00.200 --> 00:43:01.361
You know, I got a book called


00:43:01.440 --> 00:43:03.090
<i>Fundamentals of Decision Making.</i>


00:43:03.320 --> 00:43:04.401
You can borrow it.


00:43:13.240 --> 00:43:14.571
What is it?


00:43:15.600 --> 00:43:17.364
It's nothing.


00:43:17.520 --> 00:43:20.046
Looks like Mary gets to go
to Boston for a couple days.


00:43:23.880 --> 00:43:25.564
It's just two days.


00:43:26.440 --> 00:43:27.441
Relax.


00:43:37.600 --> 00:43:39.170
So, what do you think?


00:43:40.040 --> 00:43:41.405
Cool.


00:43:54.200 --> 00:43:56.362
Wow! You and my mom...


00:43:56.520 --> 00:43:58.010
were always together.


00:43:59.320 --> 00:44:00.367
Always.


00:44:21.840 --> 00:44:23.729
Oh, no, you don't want
to look at that one.


00:44:24.000 --> 00:44:25.001
Is that you?


00:44:28.600 --> 00:44:29.601
Yes.


00:44:32.160 --> 00:44:33.366
How old were you?


00:44:33.880 --> 00:44:34.881
29.


00:44:36.400 --> 00:44:38.323
Where is this?


00:44:38.480 --> 00:44:40.562
That's Cambridge University.


00:44:40.720 --> 00:44:42.722
In England.


00:44:47.560 --> 00:44:48.766
Who are those people?


00:44:48.920 --> 00:44:50.729
My research colleagues.


00:44:51.560 --> 00:44:52.721
For what?


00:44:52.880 --> 00:44:54.689
Mathematics, of course.


00:44:55.440 --> 00:44:57.044
Really?


00:44:58.920 --> 00:45:00.524
Cool!


00:45:03.080 --> 00:45:04.844
So, then you came to work...


00:45:05.000 --> 00:45:06.161
at a college in America?


00:45:06.720 --> 00:45:07.767
No.


00:45:07.920 --> 00:45:10.651
I married your grandfather...


00:45:10.800 --> 00:45:13.167
and I came back
to America with him.


00:45:14.200 --> 00:45:16.202
And I had children.


00:45:16.440 --> 00:45:17.646
Oh.


00:45:18.760 --> 00:45:19.921
So, no more math?


00:45:22.880 --> 00:45:23.927
It's late.


00:45:24.120 --> 00:45:25.849
You've got a big day tomorrow.


00:45:26.000 --> 00:45:28.970
Come on. Up, up, up.


00:45:29.160 --> 00:45:30.491
Can I play the piano?


00:45:30.560 --> 00:45:31.561
No, you can't.


00:45:31.640 --> 00:45:33.296
- Now stop dragging those feet.
- But, it's fun!


00:45:33.320 --> 00:45:34.320
Come on!


00:45:35.080 --> 00:45:38.562
I have had
a series of nightmares...


00:45:38.720 --> 00:45:41.007
where I'm fired...


00:45:42.120 --> 00:45:44.566
because of what happened.


00:45:44.800 --> 00:45:46.211
You get it?


00:45:46.800 --> 00:45:48.290
And then I try to rationalize...


00:45:48.440 --> 00:45:52.126
that everything that happened
was just all alcohol.


00:45:57.160 --> 00:45:59.003
I have an addiction
to fixer guys.


00:46:14.040 --> 00:46:15.963
Dr. Shankland,
this problem is...


00:46:16.120 --> 00:46:19.329
I know. Just copy it exactly
as you see it written.


00:46:19.640 --> 00:46:20.687
But it's...


00:46:20.920 --> 00:46:23.491
Exactly as written. Thank you.


00:46:28.840 --> 00:46:31.446
<i>So, what's this problem
I'm supposed to look at?</i>


00:46:31.520 --> 00:46:33.329
I don't know.


00:46:33.480 --> 00:46:35.767
Is it like the problems
Mom worked on?


00:46:35.920 --> 00:46:38.082
Your mother didn't work
on problems.


00:46:38.240 --> 00:46:40.402
She worked on just one problem.


00:46:40.560 --> 00:46:42.324
Just one?


00:46:42.480 --> 00:46:44.050
Her entire life?


00:46:44.200 --> 00:46:45.929
Most of it.


00:46:46.080 --> 00:46:47.286
Look.


00:46:48.960 --> 00:46:52.043
These are
the Millennium Problems.


00:46:52.840 --> 00:46:56.242
Seven great
and meaningful problems.


00:46:56.400 --> 00:46:58.482
Some mathematicians have worked


00:46:58.560 --> 00:47:00.449
their entire lives
to prove them.


00:47:01.200 --> 00:47:02.770
Who's the dude with the beard?


00:47:02.960 --> 00:47:04.371
That's not a dude.


00:47:04.520 --> 00:47:06.761
That's Grigori Perelman.


00:47:06.920 --> 00:47:09.446
He proved
the Poincare conjecture.


00:47:09.600 --> 00:47:12.683
The only one
of the seven proved.


00:47:12.840 --> 00:47:14.444
This...


00:47:16.320 --> 00:47:18.527
This is your mother's problem.


00:47:19.760 --> 00:47:20.841
Na... vi...


00:47:21.000 --> 00:47:23.731
Navier-Stokes.


00:47:25.440 --> 00:47:27.249
No picture.


00:47:27.400 --> 00:47:29.243
- She didn't solve it?
- No.


00:47:30.320 --> 00:47:31.731
She was close.


00:47:33.120 --> 00:47:35.009
She would have won
the Fields Medal...


00:47:35.680 --> 00:47:37.569
and probably shared a Nobel...


00:47:37.720 --> 00:47:40.087
considering what it would have
meant for physics.


00:47:40.240 --> 00:47:43.130
Maybe I'll have my picture
up here someday.


00:47:49.240 --> 00:47:51.004
If you really desire it...


00:47:51.160 --> 00:47:53.891
you can have
your picture there, darling.


00:47:54.040 --> 00:47:56.327
I can help you.


00:47:56.480 --> 00:48:00.246
It takes focus and hard work,
but if you succeed...


00:48:01.320 --> 00:48:04.130
your name will live forever.


00:48:14.400 --> 00:48:16.528
Don't be smug, Seymore.


00:48:16.920 --> 00:48:19.002
Well, she's had plenty of time.


00:48:19.160 --> 00:48:22.687
She traveled yesterday.
She slept in a strange bed.


00:48:23.280 --> 00:48:25.362
Give her a chance.


00:48:27.880 --> 00:48:30.201
At six years old,
she read Zimmer.


00:48:31.440 --> 00:48:32.601
Outstanding.


00:48:33.440 --> 00:48:35.681
How much did she comprehend?


00:48:37.600 --> 00:48:38.886
So, Mary...


00:48:39.920 --> 00:48:42.730
I see you're looking
at our little problem.


00:48:43.040 --> 00:48:45.247
Little? It's big.


00:48:46.000 --> 00:48:47.001
Yeah.


00:48:53.240 --> 00:48:54.969
Why are you so mad
all of a sudden?


00:48:55.160 --> 00:48:57.288
I'm not mad. I'm annoyed.


00:48:57.440 --> 00:48:58.487
Not with you, dear.


00:48:58.560 --> 00:49:00.847
With that pompous ass,
Shankland.


00:49:01.040 --> 00:49:02.769
I knew that guy was gonna
have a beard


00:49:02.840 --> 00:49:04.490
before we even went in there.


00:49:04.640 --> 00:49:06.642
Math teachers
like to grow beards.


00:49:06.800 --> 00:49:09.167
I should never have agreed
to this in the first place.


00:49:09.320 --> 00:49:10.685
Did he really expect you


00:49:10.800 --> 00:49:12.216
to just walk in
and be able to dissect...


00:49:12.240 --> 00:49:14.288
some random, massive problem?


00:49:14.440 --> 00:49:17.489
Not much to dissect,
if you ask me.


00:49:17.680 --> 00:49:19.045
Why do you say that?


00:49:19.120 --> 00:49:20.121
It was wrong.


00:49:21.120 --> 00:49:22.201
What?


00:49:22.360 --> 00:49:24.522
Well, for starters,


00:49:24.600 --> 00:49:26.762
he forgot the negative sign
on the exponent.


00:49:26.920 --> 00:49:29.002
It went downhill from there.


00:49:29.160 --> 00:49:30.730
The problem was unsolvable.


00:49:31.920 --> 00:49:35.208
Maybe this school isn't
as great as you think it is.


00:50:48.280 --> 00:50:49.930
Mary, you knew
the problem was incorrect.


00:50:50.000 --> 00:50:51.161
Why didn't you say anything?


00:50:51.360 --> 00:50:54.204
Frank says I'm not supposed to
correct older people.


00:50:56.120 --> 00:50:58.964
Nobody likes a smart-ass.


00:51:05.880 --> 00:51:08.042
I'm loaded with swag!


00:51:16.320 --> 00:51:17.560
Wanna come inside?


00:51:19.520 --> 00:51:20.521
Cat.


00:51:21.520 --> 00:51:23.682
Frank, I think this is stupid.


00:51:23.840 --> 00:51:25.888
Why don't we just call Evelyn


00:51:25.960 --> 00:51:27.320
and tell her
I don't wanna do this?


00:51:27.360 --> 00:51:28.600
Because like I told you,


00:51:28.680 --> 00:51:30.240
Evelyn didn't order this.
The court did.


00:51:30.360 --> 00:51:31.805
So again, what are we gonna do?


00:51:31.920 --> 00:51:32.967
Tell the truth.


00:51:33.040 --> 00:51:34.041
Exactly.


00:51:34.200 --> 00:51:35.456
Sooner we answer
these questions,


00:51:35.480 --> 00:51:36.561
sooner we get to go home.


00:51:36.640 --> 00:51:37.926
So, no attitude, okay?


00:51:38.080 --> 00:51:39.684
Okay.


00:51:41.560 --> 00:51:43.324
Frank?


00:51:43.480 --> 00:51:44.527
Mary.


00:51:45.840 --> 00:51:47.410
I like Evelyn.


00:51:47.560 --> 00:51:49.164
She looks like my mom.


00:51:49.320 --> 00:51:50.810
And she has a piano.


00:51:55.320 --> 00:51:57.641
But I don't wanna live with her.


00:51:57.840 --> 00:51:59.001
She's bossy.


00:52:00.320 --> 00:52:02.368
I've heard that.


00:52:02.720 --> 00:52:04.051
Hey.


00:52:05.080 --> 00:52:07.731
Don't worry.
You're not going anywhere.


00:52:09.840 --> 00:52:10.841
Promise?


00:52:13.960 --> 00:52:15.291
I promise.


00:52:15.480 --> 00:52:17.528
Hi, Mary. I'm Pat Golding,


00:52:17.600 --> 00:52:19.000
but you can call me Pat
if you like.


00:52:19.080 --> 00:52:20.730
Got it.


00:52:20.880 --> 00:52:22.644
Do you know why you're here?


00:52:22.800 --> 00:52:25.121
I mean has anyone told you
what this is about?


00:52:25.280 --> 00:52:26.840
My grandmother wants me
to live with her


00:52:26.880 --> 00:52:28.166
and I wanna stay with Frank.


00:52:28.320 --> 00:52:30.243
That's correct.


00:52:30.400 --> 00:52:32.607
I'm sure this can all be
very scary stuff.


00:52:32.680 --> 00:52:34.523
Does any of it worry you?


00:52:34.680 --> 00:52:37.650
Nope. Frank says
I'm not goin' anywhere.


00:52:38.560 --> 00:52:40.360
Your uncle told you
you're not going anywhere?


00:52:40.480 --> 00:52:42.244
Just 15 minutes ago.


00:52:42.320 --> 00:52:43.367
So, we done here?


00:52:44.960 --> 00:52:46.371
Not quite yet.


00:52:46.880 --> 00:52:49.281
My best friend other than
Frank and Fred is Roberta...


00:52:49.440 --> 00:52:50.805
who lives a couple houses away.


00:52:50.960 --> 00:52:52.086
Really? What's she like?


00:52:52.240 --> 00:52:55.403
She's nice and funny.
And I love her.


00:52:55.480 --> 00:52:57.960
That's nice.


00:52:58.120 --> 00:53:00.168
Is Roberta your only friend
your age?


00:53:00.480 --> 00:53:03.927
Roberta's not my age.
She's like 40, 50...


00:53:04.080 --> 00:53:05.730
30-something.


00:53:05.880 --> 00:53:07.689
Roberta's a grown woman?


00:53:07.840 --> 00:53:10.047
People my age are boring.


00:53:10.200 --> 00:53:11.884
Roberta's cool.


00:53:12.760 --> 00:53:13.886
Okay.


00:53:14.080 --> 00:53:15.206
I don't watch TV.


00:53:15.360 --> 00:53:17.522
But I got hooked on SpongeBob.


00:53:17.680 --> 00:53:19.648
Mostly because Roberta loves it.


00:53:21.560 --> 00:53:24.609
Oh. And on Saturday nights,
we watch the UFC.


00:53:24.800 --> 00:53:26.768
The UFC? Is that...


00:53:26.920 --> 00:53:28.081
<i>Is that Ultimate Fighting?</i>


00:53:28.240 --> 00:53:30.208
Every Saturday.


00:53:30.360 --> 00:53:32.647
<i>You and your uncle watch
Ultimate Fighting?</i>


00:53:32.800 --> 00:53:35.087
Well, you don't just watch it.


00:53:35.440 --> 00:53:36.851
Frank turns the sound down


00:53:36.920 --> 00:53:38.649
and we do the grunting
and voices.


00:53:39.480 --> 00:53:40.527
Hmm.


00:53:40.600 --> 00:53:42.523
Sometimes I attack Frank
for real.


00:53:42.680 --> 00:53:44.682
Which is really fun for me.


00:53:44.840 --> 00:53:46.808
I think if you guys knew Frank,


00:53:46.880 --> 00:53:48.370
you'd leave us alone.


00:53:49.000 --> 00:53:50.923
He can be pretty annoying...


00:53:51.120 --> 00:53:53.771
but he's a good person.


00:53:53.920 --> 00:53:55.081
I think.


00:53:56.280 --> 00:53:57.611
Why do you say that?


00:53:59.120 --> 00:54:01.441
He wanted me before I was smart.


00:54:01.880 --> 00:54:03.245
Mr. Pollard, are you...


00:54:03.400 --> 00:54:06.131
the natural father
of Mary Adler?


00:54:06.280 --> 00:54:07.770
Yes, I am.


00:54:07.920 --> 00:54:09.490
And how can you be
certain of this?


00:54:09.960 --> 00:54:13.089
Well, I always knew,
but then you had me...


00:54:13.240 --> 00:54:14.730
take a DNA test.


00:54:14.880 --> 00:54:16.484
I would offer the test results


00:54:16.560 --> 00:54:18.688
as presumptive evidence
that Mr. Pollard...


00:54:18.840 --> 00:54:21.889
is the father and natural
guardian of the minor.


00:54:22.040 --> 00:54:23.530
As well as an affidavit...


00:54:23.680 --> 00:54:25.523
from Mr. Pollard nominating...


00:54:25.680 --> 00:54:27.682
Mrs. Adler,
the maternal grandmother,


00:54:27.760 --> 00:54:29.603
as the legal guardian
of the minor.


00:54:30.400 --> 00:54:31.447
No objections.


00:54:33.600 --> 00:54:35.284
Mr. Pollard...


00:54:35.440 --> 00:54:38.922
has Mrs. Adler offered you
any monetary reward...


00:54:39.080 --> 00:54:41.560
or employment
for coming forward today?


00:54:42.280 --> 00:54:44.567
No, sir.
I have a job of my own.


00:54:44.760 --> 00:54:45.761
Thank you.


00:54:45.840 --> 00:54:47.524
No further questions,
Your Honor.


00:54:47.720 --> 00:54:48.846
Mr. Pollard...


00:54:49.000 --> 00:54:51.367
when was the last time
you saw Mary?


00:54:52.640 --> 00:54:55.120
Uh... I've never seen her.


00:54:55.200 --> 00:54:56.486
Oh, why not?


00:54:56.600 --> 00:54:58.443
By the time
I heard about Diane...


00:54:59.320 --> 00:55:01.084
Passing...


00:55:01.240 --> 00:55:03.049
the baby was gone already.


00:55:03.200 --> 00:55:05.407
Well, did you try and find her?


00:55:06.480 --> 00:55:08.084
Best I could.


00:55:08.880 --> 00:55:11.201
I couldn't just go
and search the entire country.


00:55:11.360 --> 00:55:13.408
Do you use a computer at work?


00:55:13.480 --> 00:55:14.481
Sure.


00:55:14.560 --> 00:55:16.403
You know what? Help me out.


00:55:17.960 --> 00:55:19.928
Here, let's google "Mary Adler"


00:55:20.000 --> 00:55:22.367
and, uh, see what we find.


00:55:32.720 --> 00:55:34.131
You know what?


00:55:34.280 --> 00:55:35.884
Uh, you better add
her middle name.


00:55:36.400 --> 00:55:38.164
It'll narrow it down.


00:55:42.800 --> 00:55:44.086
Eileen.


00:55:52.000 --> 00:55:53.968
Yeah. Hit Enter.


00:55:54.560 --> 00:55:55.680
Page 2.


00:55:56.120 --> 00:55:57.246
Second hit.


00:55:58.000 --> 00:56:00.606
Would you please tell
the court what you see there?


00:56:00.760 --> 00:56:02.762
It's a newspaper article called


00:56:02.880 --> 00:56:04.041
"Not So Terrible Twos. "


00:56:04.200 --> 00:56:07.761
And one of them
is Mary Eileen Adler.


00:56:07.920 --> 00:56:09.604
Same name as your daughter.


00:56:09.800 --> 00:56:12.451
Born on the same day
as your daughter.


00:56:12.600 --> 00:56:14.602
With a photograph.


00:56:14.760 --> 00:56:16.416
Um, in your defense,
you'd never recognize it...


00:56:16.440 --> 00:56:18.136
- Your Honor, this is...
- Your Honor...


00:56:18.160 --> 00:56:20.322
if there's one thing here
that's sadly obvious...


00:56:20.520 --> 00:56:23.205
it's that Mr. Pollard
has never been


00:56:23.280 --> 00:56:24.930
a genuine guardian
of the minor...


00:56:25.080 --> 00:56:26.969
and his nomination
of Mrs. Adler


00:56:27.040 --> 00:56:28.610
is no less disingenuous.


00:56:33.920 --> 00:56:35.560
While the State of Florida
gives deference


00:56:35.600 --> 00:56:37.011
to nomination
by a natural parent...


00:56:37.200 --> 00:56:38.936
I'm inclined to side
with Mr. Cullen's laptop...


00:56:38.960 --> 00:56:40.200
at this time.


00:56:40.360 --> 00:56:41.486
Thank you, Your Honor.


00:56:53.960 --> 00:56:55.041
Don't gloat.


00:56:55.200 --> 00:56:56.884
Wouldn't dream of it.


00:56:57.040 --> 00:56:58.087
Walk you to your car?


00:56:58.240 --> 00:57:00.971
We've been so preoccupied,
I'm almost ashamed to ask.


00:57:01.120 --> 00:57:03.009
How's Walter?


00:57:04.120 --> 00:57:06.122
You wouldn't believe it
if I told you.


00:57:06.200 --> 00:57:07.201
Why?


00:57:07.280 --> 00:57:11.001
Well, your stepfather
is in Montana.


00:57:11.160 --> 00:57:12.969
He bought a ranch.


00:57:13.040 --> 00:57:14.041
Bullshit.


00:57:14.120 --> 00:57:16.930
Exactly. A man whose idea
of roughing it...


00:57:17.120 --> 00:57:19.964
is being too far from the ice
machine at the Ritz-Carlton...


00:57:20.160 --> 00:57:23.323
now owns a 1,000 acres
of grass and dung.


00:57:23.480 --> 00:57:26.086
Walter Price is a cowboy.


00:57:26.240 --> 00:57:28.288
Walter Price puts on
a Brooks Brothers suit


00:57:28.360 --> 00:57:29.566
to take out the garbage.


00:57:29.720 --> 00:57:32.929
He has a cowboy hat
and cowboy boots...


00:57:33.080 --> 00:57:35.367
and a horse
that doesn't know dressage.


00:57:35.520 --> 00:57:37.284
Is there some
logical reason for this?


00:57:37.440 --> 00:57:40.046
Midlife crisis, apparently.


00:57:40.640 --> 00:57:41.641
He's 70.


00:57:41.800 --> 00:57:42.961
I know.


00:57:43.680 --> 00:57:46.160
Must have been on time delay
or something.


00:57:46.960 --> 00:57:48.041
I guess I should be happy


00:57:48.120 --> 00:57:50.521
it wasn't a 25-year-old
cocktail waitress.


00:57:51.440 --> 00:57:52.680
But then again,


00:57:52.760 --> 00:57:55.001
an affair you can explain
to friends in a minute.


00:57:55.200 --> 00:57:58.602
For this, you put on
a pot of coffee.


00:58:00.200 --> 00:58:01.645
And he's out there right now?


00:58:01.800 --> 00:58:02.847
Yessiree!


00:58:02.920 --> 00:58:06.208
Ridin' the range.
Punchin' doggies.


00:58:06.360 --> 00:58:08.601
He had a six gun on his hip...


00:58:08.760 --> 00:58:11.684
and a saddlebag full of Lipitor.


00:58:13.040 --> 00:58:16.203
The fastest asset management
in the West.


00:58:16.360 --> 00:58:18.806
The man who shot Liberty Mutual.


00:58:19.880 --> 00:58:21.882
That's what I've been
calling him.


00:58:24.600 --> 00:58:27.570
That's really, really funny.


00:58:36.040 --> 00:58:38.008
Take her to the airport.


00:58:40.880 --> 00:58:42.609
Go home, Evelyn.


00:58:42.760 --> 00:58:45.081
Or Montana.
Rustle some cattle.


00:58:47.200 --> 00:58:48.201
You know...


00:58:49.280 --> 00:58:52.329
I have no desire to hurt you.


00:58:52.480 --> 00:58:54.448
I hate it that we're at odds.


00:58:56.400 --> 00:58:57.925
We're always at odds.


00:58:59.120 --> 00:59:00.246
Yes.


00:59:01.080 --> 00:59:02.491
Hotel.


00:59:06.400 --> 00:59:08.243
Mary, baby, come on HOW.


00:59:08.320 --> 00:59:09.321
Stop this now.


00:59:09.680 --> 00:59:10.806
No.


00:59:10.960 --> 00:59:13.406
- Come on out, honey.
- No.


00:59:13.480 --> 00:59:15.376
Why did you have to tell her
that deadbeat was testifying?


00:59:15.400 --> 00:59:16.481
Because it's the truth.


00:59:16.560 --> 00:59:17.840
And if I didn't,
Evelyn would've.


00:59:17.960 --> 00:59:19.962
If I was the dad
of a little girl


00:59:20.040 --> 00:59:21.565
and I never saw her...


00:59:22.720 --> 00:59:24.961
and I was in the same town...


00:59:26.120 --> 00:59:27.451
I would visit her.


00:59:27.600 --> 00:59:29.090
Well, I hope you're happy.


00:59:32.920 --> 00:59:35.810
He didn't even need directions.


00:59:35.960 --> 00:59:38.725
He could've followed you here.


00:59:39.480 --> 00:59:41.562
Speaking of men
who aren't worth a damn.


00:59:48.040 --> 00:59:51.249
Doesn't even wanna see
what I look like.


00:59:55.400 --> 00:59:56.481
All right.


00:59:56.560 --> 00:59:58.449
Hey, put your shoes on.
We're going for a ride.


00:59:58.560 --> 00:59:59.561
You too.


01:00:00.280 --> 01:00:01.645
A ride?


01:00:02.480 --> 01:00:04.687
What are we doing here?


01:00:04.840 --> 01:00:06.524
Waiting.


01:00:06.680 --> 01:00:07.761
We can see that.


01:00:08.200 --> 01:00:09.201
Why?


01:00:09.800 --> 01:00:11.564
Because I said so.


01:00:13.640 --> 01:00:16.723
How long do we have to
stay here?


01:00:16.920 --> 01:00:18.684
As long as it takes.


01:00:18.880 --> 01:00:21.963
And keep your voice down.
It's a hospital.


01:00:25.040 --> 01:00:27.247
- Food's here.
- Yeah, food's here.


01:01:45.360 --> 01:01:47.362
It's a boy.


01:01:54.360 --> 01:01:55.361
Way to go!


01:02:04.120 --> 01:02:07.169
That's exactly how it was
when you were born.


01:02:08.720 --> 01:02:10.085
This happy?


01:02:10.440 --> 01:02:11.771
This happy-


01:02:19.720 --> 01:02:22.166
Who came out and told everybody?


01:02:24.760 --> 01:02:26.091
I did.


01:02:35.000 --> 01:02:37.048
Can we stay for another?


01:03:27.720 --> 01:03:30.291
Mrs. Adler, in your earlier
testimony, here today...


01:03:30.440 --> 01:03:32.602
you've painted a pretty dim
picture of your own son.


01:03:32.680 --> 01:03:33.806
Don't you think?


01:03:33.880 --> 01:03:35.530
I'm under oath.


01:03:35.680 --> 01:03:37.444
I take no pleasure in it.


01:03:38.200 --> 01:03:39.850
So, your son's
a failure in life,


01:03:39.960 --> 01:03:41.080
your daughter took her life.


01:03:41.120 --> 01:03:42.240
You know, you're oh for two.


01:03:42.320 --> 01:03:43.845
- Objection!
- Withdrawn.


01:03:44.000 --> 01:03:46.651
If I go one for three,
I'm in the Hall of Fame.


01:03:47.840 --> 01:03:49.763
You know baseball.


01:03:49.920 --> 01:03:50.921
Fenway Park.


01:03:51.000 --> 01:03:52.600
You know, I'd like to go there
some time.


01:03:53.000 --> 01:03:55.128
How often in a year


01:03:55.200 --> 01:03:56.850
did you take Diane
to a baseball game?


01:03:57.000 --> 01:03:58.650
Diane wasn't interested
in sports.


01:03:58.800 --> 01:04:00.928
She never wanted to go
to a game? Ever?


01:04:01.080 --> 01:04:03.651
I don't recall her ever asking.


01:04:03.800 --> 01:04:05.882
Just out of curiosity, Fenway,
that's a tough ticket.


01:04:06.040 --> 01:04:07.087
Where do you get yours?


01:04:07.280 --> 01:04:08.616
My husband has season tickets.


01:04:08.640 --> 01:04:09.880
And how long has he had them?


01:04:10.440 --> 01:04:11.487
30 years.


01:04:11.560 --> 01:04:13.688
But I've only been
married to him for 20.


01:04:13.840 --> 01:04:15.922
And Diane never went
to one game?


01:04:17.680 --> 01:04:19.887
What color was the dress
Diane wore to prom?


01:04:20.080 --> 01:04:21.650
Diane didn't attend a prom


01:04:21.720 --> 01:04:22.776
because she didn't go
to a high school.


01:04:22.800 --> 01:04:23.801
No prom.


01:04:23.920 --> 01:04:25.001
What sports did she play?


01:04:25.160 --> 01:04:26.321
As I told you earlier,


01:04:26.400 --> 01:04:28.084
she wasn't interested in sports.


01:04:28.160 --> 01:04:29.376
Did she go to camp
during the summer?


01:04:29.400 --> 01:04:30.447
No.


01:04:30.520 --> 01:04:32.682
- Community swimming pool?
- We had our own pool.


01:04:32.800 --> 01:04:34.131
- Girl Scouts?
- No.


01:04:34.280 --> 01:04:37.841
Then what did she do
with all that time?


01:04:38.000 --> 01:04:40.480
She loved mathematics.
It was her passion.


01:04:40.640 --> 01:04:43.086
She preferred it
to all other things.


01:04:43.240 --> 01:04:44.480
All other?


01:04:46.360 --> 01:04:49.603
Mrs. Adler, who's Paul Riva?


01:04:55.440 --> 01:04:56.930
He was a boy
from the neighborhood.


01:04:57.120 --> 01:04:59.487
Oh, come on.
He was much more than...


01:04:59.640 --> 01:05:01.290
just a boy
from the neighborhood.


01:05:01.440 --> 01:05:03.010
Paul was Diane's first love...


01:05:03.080 --> 01:05:04.206
wasn't he?


01:05:04.280 --> 01:05:06.362
I wouldn't characterize it
that way. No.


01:05:06.520 --> 01:05:08.363
And how would Diane
characterize it?


01:05:08.520 --> 01:05:10.568
Diane was 17 years old
at the time.


01:05:10.760 --> 01:05:12.489
She didn't know anything
about love.


01:05:13.160 --> 01:05:14.321
Mrs. Adler...


01:05:14.480 --> 01:05:16.403
in January of 1998...


01:05:16.600 --> 01:05:19.570
didn't Diane and young
Mr. Riva run away together?


01:05:19.720 --> 01:05:20.721
He coerced her.


01:05:20.880 --> 01:05:22.325
- And where did they go?
- Vermont.


01:05:22.400 --> 01:05:23.890
And you called the police,
didn't you?


01:05:23.960 --> 01:05:25.416
- Because he kidnapped her?
- Yes. Yes.


01:05:25.440 --> 01:05:27.920
And where did the police
find young Mr. Riva and Diane?


01:05:28.080 --> 01:05:29.445
I told you. Vermont.


01:05:29.600 --> 01:05:31.364
Stowe, Vermont. Wasn't it?


01:05:31.520 --> 01:05:32.521
A resort town.


01:05:32.600 --> 01:05:34.682
Stowe Mountain.


01:05:34.840 --> 01:05:36.922
He took her skiing.


01:05:37.600 --> 01:05:38.816
You see,
kidnappers don't usually


01:05:38.840 --> 01:05:40.251
take their victims skiing.


01:05:40.400 --> 01:05:44.246
But this is what Paul did...


01:05:44.400 --> 01:05:47.085
because he and Diane
were in love.


01:05:47.160 --> 01:05:48.161
No.


01:05:48.240 --> 01:05:49.480
And when they returned,


01:05:49.560 --> 01:05:51.483
you pressed kidnapping charges.


01:05:51.640 --> 01:05:54.803
You filed a lawsuit
against his parents...


01:05:54.960 --> 01:05:57.008
until Paul stopped
calling Diane.


01:05:57.160 --> 01:05:58.491
- Didn't you?
- Yes.


01:05:58.680 --> 01:06:02.287
And Diane never heard from
or saw Paul Riva again.


01:06:02.360 --> 01:06:03.361
Did she?


01:06:03.480 --> 01:06:05.209
Not to my knowledge.


01:06:07.520 --> 01:06:09.090
And how did she take it?


01:06:10.000 --> 01:06:12.367
She was upset for a while.


01:06:12.520 --> 01:06:13.681
She lost focus.


01:06:14.760 --> 01:06:16.603
She lost focus.


01:06:16.760 --> 01:06:19.331
Mrs. Adler,
in March of 1999...


01:06:19.480 --> 01:06:22.131
didn't Diane Adler attempt
to take her own life?


01:06:22.280 --> 01:06:24.248
This episode was minor.
It was nothing.


01:06:24.400 --> 01:06:26.801
I have the hospital report
in my hand.


01:06:27.000 --> 01:06:28.331
It was nothing.


01:06:28.480 --> 01:06:30.687
Diane was not like
regular people.


01:06:30.880 --> 01:06:32.086
She was extraordinary.


01:06:32.240 --> 01:06:33.571
And extraordinary people


01:06:33.640 --> 01:06:36.246
come with singular issues
and needs.


01:06:36.400 --> 01:06:39.529
You have no idea
the capability she possessed.


01:06:39.960 --> 01:06:41.405
One in a billion.


01:06:41.600 --> 01:06:44.365
And you would say, "Fine,
let's throw that away...


01:06:44.560 --> 01:06:48.610
"so the boy who cuts our yard
can make a sexual conquest. "


01:06:48.760 --> 01:06:50.489
Maybe before you make
that decision,


01:06:50.560 --> 01:06:52.085
you stand in my shoes.


01:06:52.240 --> 01:06:54.686
I had responsibilities
which went beyond


01:06:54.760 --> 01:06:56.171
the mother-daughter
relationship.


01:06:56.360 --> 01:06:58.362
The greatest discoveries


01:06:58.440 --> 01:07:00.283
which have improved life
on this planet...


01:07:00.440 --> 01:07:03.683
have come from minds
rarer than radium.


01:07:03.840 --> 01:07:06.491
Without them,
we'd still be crawling in mud.


01:07:06.640 --> 01:07:09.211
And for your information,
counselor...


01:07:09.360 --> 01:07:12.170
a year after this incident
with this boy...


01:07:12.320 --> 01:07:14.561
Diane thanked me
for my intervention.


01:07:14.960 --> 01:07:17.486
She realized she'd made
a mistake and she thanked me.


01:07:17.640 --> 01:07:19.483
You see, Diane understood
she was accountable


01:07:19.560 --> 01:07:20.766
for the gift she'd been given.


01:07:20.920 --> 01:07:22.126
And she didn't shy from it.


01:07:22.280 --> 01:07:25.204
And I think, if she were
here today, Mr. Attorney...


01:07:25.360 --> 01:07:27.840
she would refute
your baseless insinuations...


01:07:28.000 --> 01:07:29.684
that she would give up
her brilliant future


01:07:29.760 --> 01:07:30.841
and take her own life...


01:07:31.000 --> 01:07:34.607
just because Mommy didn't
get her a little red wagon.


01:07:37.080 --> 01:07:38.650
No more questions.


01:08:14.760 --> 01:08:15.841
<i>Mr. Adler...</i>


01:08:16.920 --> 01:08:18.729
where are you
currently employed?


01:08:18.880 --> 01:08:19.881
I repair boats.


01:08:19.960 --> 01:08:21.769
Oh, really? At which marina?


01:08:21.920 --> 01:08:23.809
I don't work at a marina.
I freelance.


01:08:23.960 --> 01:08:25.962
So, safe to say,
no health insurance.


01:08:26.160 --> 01:08:27.161
No.


01:08:27.520 --> 01:08:29.376
About a week before
your sister took her life...


01:08:29.400 --> 01:08:31.004
what were you doing
for a living then?


01:08:31.600 --> 01:08:32.761
I was a teacher.


01:08:33.040 --> 01:08:34.576
You're being modest, aren't you?


01:08:34.600 --> 01:08:36.568
You were a professor
at Boston University...


01:08:36.720 --> 01:08:37.801
isn't that right?


01:08:37.880 --> 01:08:39.848
Yes, well, Assistant Professor.


01:08:40.000 --> 01:08:41.411
And what'd you teach?


01:08:41.480 --> 01:08:42.481
Philosophy.


01:08:42.560 --> 01:08:44.483
Truth and logic.
That sort of thing.


01:08:45.440 --> 01:08:47.681
Your attorney said
that the primary reason...


01:08:47.840 --> 01:08:50.320
that you took Mary is because
it was what your sister...


01:08:50.520 --> 01:08:52.841
would have wanted you to do.
Is that the truth?


01:08:53.000 --> 01:08:54.001
Yes.


01:08:54.480 --> 01:08:56.200
So Diane had visited
Pinellas County before?


01:08:56.960 --> 01:08:57.961
No.


01:08:58.040 --> 01:08:59.176
Indicated she wanted
her daughter


01:08:59.200 --> 01:09:00.361
uprooted and moved here?


01:09:00.440 --> 01:09:02.204
- No.
- No.


01:09:02.360 --> 01:09:04.681
So, you decided to bring
Mary here, didn't you?


01:09:06.160 --> 01:09:07.400
Did Diane have a problem


01:09:07.480 --> 01:09:09.160
with your health plan
at Boston University?


01:09:09.200 --> 01:09:10.247
Not to my knowledge.


01:09:10.320 --> 01:09:11.416
Do you think she would want
her daughter


01:09:11.440 --> 01:09:12.576
to have access to healthcare?


01:09:12.600 --> 01:09:13.487
Of course.


01:09:13.560 --> 01:09:16.245
So what do you do,
when little Mary gets sick?


01:09:16.400 --> 01:09:17.845
You repair a doctor's boat?


01:09:18.000 --> 01:09:19.809
- Objection.
- Sustained.


01:09:20.680 --> 01:09:21.841
Mary has been identified...


01:09:22.000 --> 01:09:24.207
as a math prodigy.


01:09:24.360 --> 01:09:26.567
But her formal math education
under your care...


01:09:26.760 --> 01:09:28.922
she's learning at the
first grade level, isn't she?


01:09:29.000 --> 01:09:30.047
Yes.


01:09:30.120 --> 01:09:32.646
And you turned down
a scholarship at the Oaks...


01:09:32.720 --> 01:09:36.042
a school specializing in the
education of gifted children?


01:09:36.120 --> 01:09:37.121
Yes.


01:09:37.200 --> 01:09:39.248
And Diane,
she'd be fine with that?


01:09:41.080 --> 01:09:42.241
I couldn't say.


01:09:42.400 --> 01:09:44.176
Prior to Mrs. Adler
giving her one,


01:09:44.200 --> 01:09:45.281
did Mary have a computer?


01:09:45.360 --> 01:09:46.407
She used mine.


01:09:46.480 --> 01:09:48.642
Mr. Adler, does Diane's
daughter have her own bedroom?


01:09:48.720 --> 01:09:49.767
No.


01:09:49.840 --> 01:09:51.536
Does she sleep
in a bed that you bought...


01:09:51.560 --> 01:09:53.005
- in a secondhand shop?
- Yes.


01:09:53.160 --> 01:09:55.686
So, the truth is, Mr. Adler,


01:09:55.840 --> 01:09:57.330
that you didn't come down here


01:09:57.400 --> 01:09:58.970
because your sister
wanted you to...


01:09:59.040 --> 01:10:00.256
and you certainly
didn't come here


01:10:00.280 --> 01:10:01.440
because it was good for Mary.


01:10:01.480 --> 01:10:03.289
No, it was personal.


01:10:03.440 --> 01:10:05.124
Diane was a star.
You weren't.


01:10:05.280 --> 01:10:06.964
Diane got the attention.
You didn't.


01:10:07.120 --> 01:10:08.531
And over the years,
you got angry.


01:10:08.640 --> 01:10:09.721
And here comes Mary.


01:10:09.800 --> 01:10:11.848
What a great way to get even.


01:10:12.000 --> 01:10:13.604
You've uprooted that little girl


01:10:13.680 --> 01:10:15.364
and brought her here
for one reason only.


01:10:15.560 --> 01:10:17.403
To do harm to your mother.


01:10:17.480 --> 01:10:18.720
You blamed her for your sister.


01:10:18.760 --> 01:10:19.841
No, I don't.


01:10:19.920 --> 01:10:21.576
And Mary to you is just a pawn
in all this. Isn't she?


01:10:21.600 --> 01:10:23.648
Diane wanted Mary...


01:10:23.800 --> 01:10:25.131
to be a kid.


01:10:26.560 --> 01:10:28.608
She wanted her to have a life.


01:10:30.160 --> 01:10:31.889
She wanted her
to have friends...


01:10:32.680 --> 01:10:34.284
and to play...


01:10:35.560 --> 01:10:36.607
and to be happy.


01:10:36.760 --> 01:10:38.922
Do you realize the consequences


01:10:39.000 --> 01:10:41.002
of boredom for a gifted child,
Mr. Adler?


01:10:41.160 --> 01:10:43.288
They become resentful
and sullen.


01:10:43.440 --> 01:10:44.487
Mary's not an angry kid.


01:10:44.560 --> 01:10:45.641
Really?


01:10:45.760 --> 01:10:47.728
Did she not attack a child
on the school bus?


01:10:48.400 --> 01:10:49.526
A 12-year-old tripped


01:10:49.640 --> 01:10:51.016
a 7-year-old
and she came to his defense.


01:10:51.040 --> 01:10:52.963
- Did she break the boy's nose?
- Yes.


01:10:53.120 --> 01:10:57.125
On October 16th of last year
were you arrested for assault?


01:10:57.280 --> 01:10:58.520
Oh, my God.


01:10:58.800 --> 01:11:00.840
You have to answer
the question, Mr. Adler.


01:11:02.800 --> 01:11:06.122
A drunk idiot attacked me
and I defended myself.


01:11:06.320 --> 01:11:07.376
What does that have to do
with anything?


01:11:07.400 --> 01:11:08.680
Did you spend the night in jail?


01:11:09.440 --> 01:11:10.521
Yeah.


01:11:10.600 --> 01:11:12.648
You are in way
over your head here.


01:11:12.800 --> 01:11:14.245
You're depriving that girl.


01:11:14.400 --> 01:11:15.696
You're gambling
with her future...


01:11:15.720 --> 01:11:17.776
and now you're being presented
with an opportunity...


01:11:17.800 --> 01:11:18.976
to do right by her.
Jump at it.


01:11:19.000 --> 01:11:20.336
Does counsel
have a question for my client?


01:11:20.360 --> 01:11:21.771
Take the high road,
Mr. Adler...


01:11:21.880 --> 01:11:23.016
before she is
irreparably damaged.


01:11:23.040 --> 01:11:24.136
Does counsel have a question...


01:11:24.160 --> 01:11:25.176
- for my client or not?
- Yes, sir.


01:11:25.200 --> 01:11:26.850
I do have the question.


01:11:28.520 --> 01:11:31.000
Tell us, is your
continued guardianship...


01:11:31.160 --> 01:11:34.323
really in the best interest
of this little girl?


01:11:41.240 --> 01:11:42.366
Yes.


01:11:43.040 --> 01:11:44.041
Yes, it is.


01:11:44.640 --> 01:11:46.563
I have no further questions.


01:11:54.240 --> 01:11:55.416
Research and Development...


01:11:55.440 --> 01:11:57.044
has come up
with a brand new Fred cheer.


01:11:57.200 --> 01:12:00.170
Fred personally asked me
if I would tell you it.


01:12:00.320 --> 01:12:02.209
Let's hear it.


01:12:02.360 --> 01:12:05.569
<i>S - O - C - K - I - T
Sock it to me, Freddy...</i>


01:12:05.720 --> 01:12:08.041
<i>Sock it.</i>


01:12:09.560 --> 01:12:11.881
<i>Sock it.</i>


01:12:15.600 --> 01:12:17.170
Tell R and D, they got a winner.


01:12:17.320 --> 01:12:19.482
That's exactly what I said.


01:12:20.680 --> 01:12:24.127
<i>S - O - C - K - I - T
Sock it to me, Freddy</i>


01:12:26.680 --> 01:12:28.648
They wanna cut a deal.


01:12:30.880 --> 01:12:32.803
Highsmith called me
first thing this morning.


01:12:32.960 --> 01:12:34.560
Why would he do that?
I don't understand.


01:12:34.600 --> 01:12:35.965
In the middle of...


01:12:36.160 --> 01:12:38.561
Just listen.
Listen to me, man.


01:12:41.240 --> 01:12:44.608
Mary would be put
in a fostering situation.


01:12:44.760 --> 01:12:45.886
No.


01:12:46.040 --> 01:12:47.256
- Come on, Frank.
- Cullen, I told you no.


01:12:47.280 --> 01:12:48.645
It wouldn't be
a court-appointed


01:12:48.760 --> 01:12:50.046
foster family, Frank.


01:12:50.200 --> 01:12:51.616
- Hey! Drop it!
- We could cherry-pick...


01:12:51.640 --> 01:12:52.766
from the cream of the crop.


01:12:52.840 --> 01:12:54.490
Mutually approved.


01:12:55.000 --> 01:12:56.650
Just hear me out.


01:12:56.720 --> 01:12:57.767
Tampa.


01:12:57.840 --> 01:12:59.888
I insisted, and they agreed.


01:13:00.040 --> 01:13:02.646
No more than a half an hour
from your front door.


01:13:02.800 --> 01:13:04.723
Now, she would attend the Oaks.


01:13:04.880 --> 01:13:06.530
It's a great school.


01:13:06.680 --> 01:13:08.320
And visiting rights
for the grandmother...


01:13:08.440 --> 01:13:09.885
but she was gonna
get that anyway.


01:13:10.040 --> 01:13:12.042
Right? And on her
12th birthday, Frank,


01:13:12.120 --> 01:13:13.406
she can go back into court...


01:13:13.560 --> 01:13:14.641
- No.
- And decide then...


01:13:14.720 --> 01:13:15.896
where she wants to live
and with who.


01:13:15.920 --> 01:13:16.807
I don't understand this.


01:13:16.880 --> 01:13:18.216
I thought you were supposed
to be on my team.


01:13:18.240 --> 01:13:19.416
Why are you bringing me
this deal?


01:13:19.440 --> 01:13:21.442
Other than
I'm required to by law?


01:13:21.600 --> 01:13:23.011
You like this deal?


01:13:24.640 --> 01:13:26.165
I love this deal.


01:13:43.920 --> 01:13:45.604
They think they're gonna lose.


01:13:46.160 --> 01:13:47.605
Yeah.


01:13:47.760 --> 01:13:48.886
They do.


01:13:50.320 --> 01:13:51.810
You think we're gonna lose.


01:13:52.080 --> 01:13:53.161
Yes.


01:13:53.360 --> 01:13:55.044
I do, Frank.


01:14:02.760 --> 01:14:05.331
I gotta go put my kids to bed.


01:14:06.960 --> 01:14:09.201
I'll do whatever
you want me to do.


01:14:10.000 --> 01:14:13.402
But if we leave this
up to that judge, Nichols...


01:14:13.560 --> 01:14:15.562
he's old school, Frank.


01:14:15.760 --> 01:14:17.842
Does he like your mother? No.


01:14:18.000 --> 01:14:19.331
Does he like her income?


01:14:19.480 --> 01:14:22.529
Does he like her health plan?
Does he like her home?


01:14:22.680 --> 01:14:24.648
You better believe it.


01:14:24.800 --> 01:14:26.529
I've been in his courtroom.


01:14:26.680 --> 01:14:28.250
A hundred times.


01:14:29.400 --> 01:14:31.209
And if it's a coin toss...


01:14:31.400 --> 01:14:32.526
Look at me.


01:14:35.480 --> 01:14:38.245
If it's a coin toss...


01:14:38.400 --> 01:14:42.325
that old boy is going to
side with the money.


01:14:43.160 --> 01:14:45.162
So, do me a favor, Frank.


01:14:45.320 --> 01:14:48.051
Just meet the family.
See how it feels.


01:14:48.200 --> 01:14:49.565
It's all I ask.


01:15:03.840 --> 01:15:09.761
<i>Fly away, little pretty bird</i>


01:15:11.920 --> 01:15:16.562
<i>Fly, fly away...</i>


01:15:17.600 --> 01:15:20.046
Pool. Florida.


01:15:20.880 --> 01:15:23.360
That dock
is on the Intercoastal.


01:15:23.520 --> 01:15:25.284
Which I guess is obvious...


01:15:25.440 --> 01:15:27.442
since we're on the Intercoastal.


01:15:30.040 --> 01:15:32.281
Added this desk,
so she could do her homework.


01:15:32.440 --> 01:15:33.965
Yeah.


01:15:34.160 --> 01:15:36.447
And this would be her room.


01:15:38.140 --> 01:15:44.044
<i>I see in your eyes a promise</i>


01:15:45.120 --> 01:15:48.124
So, while I'm trying to
sell you on the house...


01:15:48.280 --> 01:15:49.964
and us...


01:15:50.120 --> 01:15:51.690
I just don't want you to think


01:15:51.760 --> 01:15:53.489
that we're
completely insensitive...


01:15:53.640 --> 01:15:55.324
to what you're feeling.


01:16:06.080 --> 01:16:08.560
You guys gonna be okay
with a cat?


01:16:10.440 --> 01:16:12.204
Absolutely.


01:16:14.400 --> 01:16:18.962
<i>Love's own tender flames</i>


01:16:19.320 --> 01:16:21.482
<i>Warm this meeting</i>


01:16:23.000 --> 01:16:28.907
<i>And love's tender song
you will sing</i>


01:16:31.120 --> 01:16:34.283
But fly away...


01:16:34.400 --> 01:16:37.688
I've been thinking a lot
about the word "compromise. "


01:16:37.840 --> 01:16:41.322
On one hand,
good challenging school...


01:16:41.480 --> 01:16:42.811
on the other...


01:16:43.280 --> 01:16:44.645
foster people.


01:16:44.800 --> 01:16:46.404
They can watch sitcoms with her.


01:16:46.560 --> 01:16:48.483
Take her to Olive Garden.


01:16:48.640 --> 01:16:51.291
Teach her
to say "irregardless. "


01:16:51.440 --> 01:16:53.169
The only saving grace,
I suppose,


01:16:53.240 --> 01:16:55.288
is she's better off
than she was.


01:16:58.160 --> 01:16:59.366
Well...


01:17:01.800 --> 01:17:03.404
Goodbye, Frank.


01:17:16.720 --> 01:17:18.404
Hey.


01:17:18.560 --> 01:17:20.130
<i>Come on.</i>


01:17:20.320 --> 01:17:21.970
I'm only 25 minutes away.


01:17:22.120 --> 01:17:24.168
Please don't leave me here.


01:17:24.320 --> 01:17:25.731
- Please.
- No.


01:17:27.280 --> 01:17:28.327
Look, you're going to


01:17:28.400 --> 01:17:29.811
a brand new school,
a better school.


01:17:29.960 --> 01:17:31.724
I don't want to.


01:17:31.880 --> 01:17:33.041
I want my crummy school.


01:17:33.200 --> 01:17:34.440
- And you got Fred.
- Please.


01:17:34.600 --> 01:17:35.936
And once a month
you can come back.


01:17:35.960 --> 01:17:37.096
You can stay with me
and Roberta.


01:17:37.120 --> 01:17:39.168
I want you and Roberta now!


01:17:39.320 --> 01:17:41.084
And in a few years,
if you want...


01:17:41.240 --> 01:17:42.844
you can come back.
You can live with me.


01:17:43.320 --> 01:17:44.685
I wanna stay with you.


01:17:44.840 --> 01:17:46.330
Frank, you promised me.


01:17:46.480 --> 01:17:48.482
- Come on. Don't do this.
- You promised me.


01:17:48.680 --> 01:17:49.806
I know.


01:17:50.560 --> 01:17:51.641
I know.


01:17:52.240 --> 01:17:54.891
Please, Frank.
Why are you leaving me?


01:17:55.040 --> 01:17:58.010
Because the court said
I had to. You know this.


01:17:58.160 --> 01:18:00.003
We've discussed this ad naus...


01:18:02.200 --> 01:18:05.090
We've discussed this. Come on.


01:18:06.920 --> 01:18:08.570
- Come on, please.
- No!


01:18:08.640 --> 01:18:09.766
- Hey! Mary.
- No!


01:18:09.840 --> 01:18:10.921
Hey, Mary.


01:18:11.040 --> 01:18:12.166
No! No!


01:18:12.320 --> 01:18:13.446
Sweetheart, you know what?


01:18:13.600 --> 01:18:14.681
No!


01:18:14.880 --> 01:18:16.291
There's no easy way to do this.


01:18:16.440 --> 01:18:18.249
Not gonna be as long
as you think, honey.


01:18:18.400 --> 01:18:19.561
- Frank!
- You're gonna see.


01:18:19.720 --> 01:18:21.006
Frank!


01:18:21.280 --> 01:18:23.203
Don't leave me!


01:18:23.360 --> 01:18:25.442
- I know this is hard.
- Please!


01:18:25.600 --> 01:18:28.001
No! Get your hands off of me!


01:18:28.160 --> 01:18:30.128
- Frank! Please!
- I know it's hard.


01:18:30.280 --> 01:18:32.089
- Come back!
- Mary! I know.


01:18:32.240 --> 01:18:33.446
No!


01:18:33.640 --> 01:18:35.324
Frank!


01:18:35.800 --> 01:18:37.404
Don't go!


01:18:38.760 --> 01:18:40.410
I need you!


01:18:40.560 --> 01:18:42.881
Fred needs you!


01:18:43.200 --> 01:18:44.440
You promised me!


01:18:51.200 --> 01:18:52.247
No!


01:19:06.720 --> 01:19:08.290
Huh.


01:19:32.040 --> 01:19:33.451
Hey, down there.


01:19:36.080 --> 01:19:37.760
I don't know
which mistake is worse.


01:19:37.800 --> 01:19:39.370
Designing a water pump
that leaks...


01:19:39.520 --> 01:19:42.330
or putting it somewhere
no human being can reach.


01:19:46.360 --> 01:19:48.886
How do you design something
you know is gonna fail?


01:19:50.280 --> 01:19:53.284
Gotta be devious
or clueless, right?


01:19:58.640 --> 01:20:00.324
After the first few weeks,
I knew...


01:20:00.520 --> 01:20:02.522
I had to find
a real family for her.


01:20:05.680 --> 01:20:08.126
I was in way over my head.


01:20:11.560 --> 01:20:15.007
And every day, I'd say,
"Today's the day...


01:20:15.200 --> 01:20:17.043
"I'm takin' her
to child services. "


01:20:17.200 --> 01:20:19.965
And every day,
she'd do something just...


01:20:23.520 --> 01:20:26.000
so unbelievably cool.


01:20:27.480 --> 01:20:30.165
Her little personality
was exploding.


01:20:32.080 --> 01:20:33.764
She was funny.


01:20:34.720 --> 01:20:37.451
And she was angry, and
she was happy, and she was...


01:20:38.600 --> 01:20:40.045
sad.


01:20:41.360 --> 01:20:42.441
And was cute.


01:20:44.280 --> 01:20:46.442
Just so damn entertaining.


01:20:46.600 --> 01:20:48.443
And so I kept her.


01:20:48.600 --> 01:20:50.125
Not that
that's in her best interest.


01:20:50.320 --> 01:20:52.926
Not that I'm capable
of raising a child.


01:20:53.080 --> 01:20:54.680
A child that might still
have a mother...


01:20:54.720 --> 01:20:57.200
if I had taken the time to
notice that she needed me.


01:20:59.560 --> 01:21:02.609
And now,
six and a half years later...


01:21:02.760 --> 01:21:04.649
I finally got her
to the foster family,


01:21:04.720 --> 01:21:06.051
and you know what?


01:21:06.200 --> 01:21:08.282
It was great. She loved it.


01:21:08.920 --> 01:21:10.968
I thought
it would be a nightmare...


01:21:11.120 --> 01:21:12.610
of abandonment and betrayal.


01:21:12.720 --> 01:21:14.882
But, turns out
it was a huge success.


01:21:16.160 --> 01:21:17.241
I'm a fucking hero.


01:21:23.520 --> 01:21:25.204
- Frank...
- No, Bonnie.


01:21:26.040 --> 01:21:27.804
I appreciate
everything you've done.


01:21:27.960 --> 01:21:29.200
Just"


01:21:48.320 --> 01:21:50.084
- Hey.
- Hi, Frank.


01:21:52.320 --> 01:21:54.368
We're having a little bit
of a problem in there.


01:21:54.720 --> 01:21:55.721
What?


01:21:55.880 --> 01:21:57.848
Uh, Mary's fine...


01:21:58.000 --> 01:21:59.889
but she's having
a little bit of a meltdown.


01:22:00.760 --> 01:22:02.922
Right. Let me talk to her.


01:22:03.080 --> 01:22:04.491
No, hang on.


01:22:05.200 --> 01:22:07.646
That's not a good idea.


01:22:08.000 --> 01:22:11.129
Your visit here is the reason
for the meltdown.


01:22:11.400 --> 01:22:12.526
What?


01:22:13.880 --> 01:22:15.882
She don't wanna see you.


01:22:21.120 --> 01:22:22.645
I'm sorry, man.


01:22:23.400 --> 01:22:25.050
This is predictable.


01:22:25.200 --> 01:22:27.726
You know, she needs time.


01:22:33.160 --> 01:22:34.810
Just give me five minutes
with her.


01:22:35.360 --> 01:22:36.691
I let you inside...


01:22:36.840 --> 01:22:38.569
then we're gonna
betray her trust


01:22:38.680 --> 01:22:40.170
and we have
an even bigger problem.


01:23:56.480 --> 01:23:57.811
Oh...


01:25:05.720 --> 01:25:07.131
- Hi.
- Hi! Can we help you?


01:25:07.240 --> 01:25:09.766
Yeah. Do you have a one-eyed
orange cat named Fred?


01:25:11.680 --> 01:25:13.170
We have a one-eyed cat,


01:25:13.240 --> 01:25:14.560
but I don't know
what his name is.


01:25:14.680 --> 01:25:16.011
Where?


01:25:16.160 --> 01:25:18.561
I don't know.
Today was his last day.


01:25:21.080 --> 01:25:22.650
Hey, you can't go back there.


01:25:26.280 --> 01:25:27.281
Hey.


01:25:29.720 --> 01:25:32.166
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
what are you doing back here?


01:25:36.400 --> 01:25:38.528
I told him he couldn't.


01:25:42.880 --> 01:25:43.881
Hey, Fred.


01:25:47.160 --> 01:25:48.685
Who brought this cat in?


01:25:48.840 --> 01:25:51.207
Some guy. He said
it was an allergy issue.


01:25:54.360 --> 01:25:55.964
Evelyn.


01:26:38.120 --> 01:26:39.406
- Frank!
- Where's Evelyn?


01:26:39.560 --> 01:26:40.925
Evelyn? You mean your mother?


01:26:41.080 --> 01:26:42.650
- Yes.
- Kevin.


01:26:42.840 --> 01:26:44.171
Evelyn is in the guest house.


01:26:44.320 --> 01:26:46.402
Yeah, listen. I'm sorry, man.


01:26:46.560 --> 01:26:47.846
Frank, let me tell you,


01:26:47.920 --> 01:26:49.888
she was so helpful
with the tutors.


01:26:50.040 --> 01:26:51.280
- Mary was so distant.
- Hey!


01:26:51.440 --> 01:26:52.656
Look, we know
what you're up against.


01:26:52.680 --> 01:26:53.696
Do you want your life back?


01:26:53.720 --> 01:26:54.720
Go back inside.


01:26:59.800 --> 01:27:01.006
What are you doing here?


01:27:03.480 --> 01:27:04.845
Come on, Mary.
We're goin' home.


01:27:05.000 --> 01:27:07.526
- No.
- You're trespassing!


01:27:09.440 --> 01:27:10.805
You need to look at this.


01:27:11.400 --> 01:27:12.400
Let's go, Mary.


01:27:12.440 --> 01:27:13.601
- Let's move. Come on.
- No!


01:27:13.680 --> 01:27:14.761
- Hey! Mary.
- Mary!


01:27:14.920 --> 01:27:16.001
Mary!


01:27:16.200 --> 01:27:18.487
- It's okay. I got her.
- Uh-uh!


01:27:20.360 --> 01:27:22.522
Think again, lady.


01:27:45.200 --> 01:27:46.326
Mary!


01:27:46.480 --> 01:27:48.642
Mary! Hey, stop it.


01:27:48.800 --> 01:27:50.165
No! Let me go!


01:27:50.320 --> 01:27:51.401
No!


01:27:51.560 --> 01:27:53.244
- No! No!
'Stop, Mary!


01:27:53.400 --> 01:27:54.845
- Stop. Stop
- No!


01:27:55.040 --> 01:27:56.485
- Come here.
- You lied to me!


01:27:56.640 --> 01:27:57.641
I know!


01:27:57.760 --> 01:28:00.286
- No! No!
'Stop! Stop, Stop!


01:28:00.520 --> 01:28:01.806
I'm sorry.


01:28:02.000 --> 01:28:04.606
I made a mistake.
I'm so sorry.


01:28:04.800 --> 01:28:05.926
You promised me.


01:28:06.080 --> 01:28:07.161
I know.


01:28:07.320 --> 01:28:08.481
You promised.


01:28:08.560 --> 01:28:10.847
I know. I'm sorry.


01:28:12.160 --> 01:28:13.605
You said you wouldn't leave me.


01:28:13.880 --> 01:28:15.405
I made a mistake.


01:28:16.440 --> 01:28:18.647
I'm sorry.


01:28:21.840 --> 01:28:23.808
I was so sad!


01:28:25.080 --> 01:28:26.161
I missed you.


01:28:26.360 --> 01:28:27.964
I missed you, too.


01:28:29.160 --> 01:28:30.889
They took Fred.


01:28:31.040 --> 01:28:33.566
No. It's okay.


01:28:33.720 --> 01:28:36.485
- I got him. He's home.
- What?


01:28:36.640 --> 01:28:39.166
He's at the apartment
right now. I got him.


01:28:39.840 --> 01:28:41.046
For real?


01:28:41.160 --> 01:28:44.767
Yeah. He's home kicking around
his ping pong ball.


01:28:45.840 --> 01:28:47.888
Why did you leave me there?


01:28:49.440 --> 01:28:51.681
Because I thought
I was bad for you.


01:28:52.800 --> 01:28:54.325
And then it dawned on me.


01:28:54.480 --> 01:28:56.926
If Mary is this amazing...


01:28:57.080 --> 01:29:00.209
smart, sweet human being...


01:29:00.360 --> 01:29:02.442
then I must be
doing something right.


01:29:10.880 --> 01:29:13.167
You're smiling.


01:29:24.920 --> 01:29:26.649
Roberta!


01:29:27.560 --> 01:29:28.607
Oh, baby.


01:29:28.680 --> 01:29:30.603
Of all the stunts
you could pull.


01:29:31.560 --> 01:29:33.130
- Where are they going?
- Nowhere.


01:29:33.280 --> 01:29:34.361
Not yet.


01:29:35.440 --> 01:29:36.771
You two, out!


01:29:43.160 --> 01:29:44.576
- What is this?
- Do you want to know...


01:29:44.600 --> 01:29:45.696
how Diane told me she finished?


01:29:45.720 --> 01:29:47.722
What is this unconscionable lie?


01:29:47.880 --> 01:29:49.120
I walked into her apartment


01:29:49.200 --> 01:29:50.296
and she was sitting
on the floor...


01:29:50.320 --> 01:29:51.367
with that baby in her arms


01:29:51.440 --> 01:29:52.576
and you know
what she said to me?


01:29:52.600 --> 01:29:54.090
Admit it. You made this up.


01:29:54.280 --> 01:29:55.770
- She said, "What do I do now?"
- No.


01:29:55.920 --> 01:29:57.285
It is not a completed proof...


01:29:57.440 --> 01:30:00.091
- It is.
- No! It isn't! It can't be.


01:30:00.240 --> 01:30:01.480
Evelyn, stop!


01:30:03.040 --> 01:30:04.530
I'm taking Mary
and I'm raising her


01:30:04.600 --> 01:30:06.125
how I believe Diane
would've wanted.


01:30:06.280 --> 01:30:07.496
- We'll see about that later.
- I realize...


01:30:07.520 --> 01:30:08.851
she's not normal.


01:30:08.920 --> 01:30:10.968
But if Einstein can
ride a bike, so can she.


01:30:11.120 --> 01:30:13.600
Let's just say Diane didn't
tell me, which is nonsense...


01:30:13.800 --> 01:30:15.006
it's a Millennium Problem.


01:30:15.080 --> 01:30:16.923
She would have shared it
with the world.


01:30:17.080 --> 01:30:18.844
That's where
your charade falls apart.


01:30:19.000 --> 01:30:20.968
If she had completed the proof,


01:30:21.040 --> 01:30:22.451
she would have published it.


01:30:25.480 --> 01:30:27.767
Diane instructed me
very clearly.


01:30:30.400 --> 01:30:32.368
That I was only to publish it
postmortem.


01:30:32.960 --> 01:30:34.610
She died six years ago.


01:30:37.560 --> 01:30:39.483
It wasn't her death
she was talking about.


01:30:59.960 --> 01:31:02.167
I tried to talk her out of it.


01:31:03.720 --> 01:31:05.131
But you know how Diane could be


01:31:05.200 --> 01:31:07.043
when she made her mind up
about something.


01:31:08.720 --> 01:31:10.449
I called MIT.


01:31:10.520 --> 01:31:11.601
Shankland's out of his mind


01:31:11.680 --> 01:31:13.682
about the possibility
of publishing it with you.


01:31:15.080 --> 01:31:16.525
He's waiting for your call.


01:31:17.440 --> 01:31:19.536
You're gonna be spending the
next few years of your life...


01:31:19.560 --> 01:31:21.005
defending it.


01:31:21.440 --> 01:31:22.965
You won't have time for her.


01:31:29.280 --> 01:31:30.964
What if I say no?


01:31:37.480 --> 01:31:39.244
Back to Plan A.


01:31:43.240 --> 01:31:45.607
Wait for me to die?


01:31:50.200 --> 01:31:53.329
I know Diane was hard.


01:31:56.560 --> 01:31:57.925
I know she was angry.


01:31:59.520 --> 01:32:02.046
But something really good
came out of this, Evelyn.


01:32:05.880 --> 01:32:07.564
She needs you now.


01:32:08.440 --> 01:32:10.522
You're the best woman
for the job.


01:32:11.120 --> 01:32:12.531
Take it.


01:32:17.640 --> 01:32:21.326
It doesn't seem as though
Diane wanted me to have it.


01:32:25.560 --> 01:32:27.688
Diane didn't always
think things through.


01:32:32.640 --> 01:32:33.846
I'll be outside.


01:32:35.000 --> 01:32:36.331
Let me know what you wanna do.


01:33:56.800 --> 01:33:57.896
You've reached


01:33:57.920 --> 01:34:00.366
<i>the Department
of Mathematics at MIT.</i>


01:34:00.520 --> 01:34:01.931
<i>If you know
your party's extension,</i>


01:34:02.000 --> 01:34:04.082
<i>you may dial it at any time.</i>


01:34:05.280 --> 01:34:06.884
<i>If you wish to speak
to an operator...</i>


01:34:06.960 --> 01:34:08.041
<i>please stay on the line</i>


01:34:08.160 --> 01:34:10.447
<i>and someone will be with you
as soon as possible.</i>


01:34:17.680 --> 01:34:20.081
Good afternoon, MIT Mathematics,


01:34:20.160 --> 01:34:21.321
<i>how may I direct your call?</i>


01:34:22.680 --> 01:34:25.081
<i>Hello? I'm sorry.
I can't hear you very well.</i>


01:34:25.240 --> 01:34:27.083
No! No.


01:34:27.840 --> 01:34:29.808
<i>Yeah. There you are.</i>


01:34:29.960 --> 01:34:31.246
<i>Yeah, can I help you?</i>


01:34:31.400 --> 01:34:32.606
Uh, yes.


01:34:35.280 --> 01:34:37.044
Doctor Shankland.


01:34:37.560 --> 01:34:39.722
<i>I'm really sorry.
I can't hear you.</i>


01:34:39.880 --> 01:34:41.723
<i>Could you speak up, please?</i>


01:34:44.760 --> 01:34:45.807
<i>Hello?</i>


01:34:49.680 --> 01:34:52.047
Evelyn Adler...


01:34:52.200 --> 01:34:54.123
for Seymore Shankland, please.


01:34:56.160 --> 01:34:57.416
And what I want you to notice,


01:34:57.440 --> 01:34:58.885
is that when you
compute P of N...


01:34:59.040 --> 01:35:00.963
for N congruent
to four mod five...


01:35:01.120 --> 01:35:03.851
the answer
is a multiple of five.


01:35:04.000 --> 01:35:05.889
So, the first person
to notice this


01:35:05.960 --> 01:35:07.086
was Srinivasa Ramanujan.


01:35:07.240 --> 01:35:08.810
In the beginning
of the 20th century...


01:35:08.960 --> 01:35:11.327
he proved that
it was the case for all...


01:35:11.480 --> 01:35:13.369
numbers congruent
to four mod five.


01:35:13.560 --> 01:35:16.530
So, he proved
that P of five N plus four...


01:35:16.680 --> 01:35:18.842
is congruent
to zero mod seven...


01:35:19.000 --> 01:35:21.606
and that P of eleven N plus six


01:35:21.680 --> 01:35:23.523
is congruent to zero mod eleven.


01:35:27.600 --> 01:35:28.647
Good?


01:35:33.520 --> 01:35:35.124
You drive like an old lady.


01:35:35.280 --> 01:35:36.720
It's Florida.
I'm blending in.


01:35:37.720 --> 01:35:39.085
How was school?


01:35:39.440 --> 01:35:41.204
Hmm, fun.


01:35:41.360 --> 01:35:43.840
Not like regular school fun...


01:35:44.000 --> 01:35:45.684
but interesting.


01:35:48.840 --> 01:35:50.649
What is this book?


01:35:50.800 --> 01:35:53.770
<i>Discourse on Method.
Rene Descartes.</i>


01:35:54.360 --> 01:35:55.885
What's it about?


01:35:56.040 --> 01:35:57.565
Existence.


01:35:57.640 --> 01:35:58.766
Existence?


01:35:58.840 --> 01:36:01.889
Yup. "I think,
therefore I am. "


01:36:02.440 --> 01:36:04.010
Well, of course you are.


01:36:04.080 --> 01:36:05.570
That's obvious.


01:36:08.480 --> 01:36:12.451
I think about Fred,
therefore, I am.


01:36:12.600 --> 01:36:14.682
<i>Cogito ergo Fred?</i>


01:36:14.840 --> 01:36:18.367
He's a dude and he's a guy.


01:36:18.520 --> 01:36:21.524
And he only has one eye.


01:36:23.160 --> 01:36:25.640
Fred, Fred, Fred!


01:36:26.600 --> 01:36:28.364
Freddy, Fred, Fred!


01:36:33.000 --> 01:36:34.525
All right, here we are.


01:36:34.720 --> 01:36:36.563
Hey! Wait till
I come to a stop.


01:36:36.720 --> 01:36:39.087
